  "learningJourneySeerahEarlyLifeTitle": "Early Life of the Prophet ﷺ",
  "learningJourneySeerahEarlyLifeIntro": "The early life of the Prophet Muhammad ﷺ teaches trust in Allah, quiet preparation, and noble character before public prophethood.",
  "learningJourneySeerahEarlyLifeSection1Title": "Key events",
  "learningJourneySeerahEarlyLifeSection1Body": "He ﷺ was born in Makkah, lost his father before birth, lost his mother in childhood, and was then cared for by his grandfather and uncle. These early losses did not diminish him. Allah cared for him and prepared him.",
  "learningJourneySeerahEarlyLifeSection2Title": "Lessons from the early years",
  "learningJourneySeerahEarlyLifeSection2Body": "Before revelation, people already knew him as truthful and trustworthy. The early Seerah shows that prophetic character was visible long before public mission.",
  "learningJourneySeerahEarlyLifeBullet1": "Hardship can refine a person instead of destroying them.",
  "learningJourneySeerahEarlyLifeBullet2": "Truthfulness and trust are foundations of da‘wah.",
  "learningJourneySeerahEarlyLifeBullet3": "Allah prepares people long before a visible mission begins.",
  "learningJourneySeerahEarlyLifeTakeaway1": "The Prophet ﷺ grew under Allah’s care through hardship and dignity.",
  "learningJourneySeerahEarlyLifeTakeaway2": "Character is part of preparation for leadership.",
  "learningJourneySeerahEarlyLifeTakeaway3": "The early Seerah teaches patience without self-pity.",
  "learningJourneySeerahEarlyLifeReflection": "Which quality from the Prophet’s ﷺ early life would most strengthen your own character right now?",
  "learningJourneySeerahFirstRevelationTitle": "First Revelation",
  "learningJourneySeerahFirstRevelationIntro": "The first revelation opened the mission of prophethood with a call to read in the name of Allah.",
  "learningJourneySeerahFirstRevelationSection1Title": "What happened in Hira",
  "learningJourneySeerahFirstRevelationSection1Body": "The Prophet ﷺ sought quiet reflection in the cave of Hira. There Jibril came with the first revelation and the command to read in the name of the Lord who created.",
  "learningJourneySeerahFirstRevelationSection2Title": "Why this moment matters",
  "learningJourneySeerahFirstRevelationSection2Body": "The beginning of revelation joined knowledge, worship, humility, and awe. It was a heavy moment, yet it became mercy for the world.",
  "learningJourneySeerahFirstRevelationBullet1": "Revelation began with knowledge connected to Allah.",
  "learningJourneySeerahFirstRevelationBullet2": "The Prophet ﷺ felt the weight of responsibility, not pride.",
  "learningJourneySeerahFirstRevelationBullet3": "The Qur’an entered history gradually and purposefully.",
  "learningJourneySeerahFirstRevelationTakeaway1": "Knowledge in Islam begins in the name of Allah.",
  "learningJourneySeerahFirstRevelationTakeaway2": "The first revelation teaches humility before responsibility.",
  "learningJourneySeerahFirstRevelationTakeaway3": "The Qur’an is revelation, not human wisdom.",
  "learningJourneySeerahFirstRevelationReflection": "How would your approach to learning change if you began it consciously in the name of Allah?",
  "learningJourneySeerahMakkahTitle": "Makkah Period",
  "learningJourneySeerahMakkahIntro": "The Makkan years were years of tawheed, patience, sacrifice, and steady calling under pressure.",
  "learningJourneySeerahMakkahSection1Title": "The Makkan call",
  "learningJourneySeerahMakkahSection1Body": "In Makkah the Prophet ﷺ called people to worship Allah alone while facing mockery, pressure, and persecution. The early believers were formed in a difficult environment.",
  "learningJourneySeerahMakkahSection2Title": "What Makkah built",
  "learningJourneySeerahMakkahSection2Body": "The Makkan Qur’an built belief first: who Allah is, what the Hereafter means, why worship matters, and how patience steadies the heart.",
  "learningJourneySeerahMakkahBullet1": "Belief is strengthened before public power arrives.",
  "learningJourneySeerahMakkahBullet2": "Patience in truth is part of the prophetic path.",
  "learningJourneySeerahMakkahBullet3": "The Qur’an shaped hearts before society was reshaped.",
  "learningJourneySeerahMakkahTakeaway1": "The Makkan years centered tawheed and endurance.",
  "learningJourneySeerahMakkahTakeaway2": "Strong worship often begins in difficult conditions.",
  "learningJourneySeerahMakkahTakeaway3": "Early believers were trained through pressure and sincerity.",
  "learningJourneySeerahMakkahReflection": "When your beliefs feel tested, what helps you stay gentle and steady instead of reactive?",
  "learningJourneySeerahHijrahTitle": "Hijrah",
  "learningJourneySeerahHijrahIntro": "Hijrah was a move for worship, safety, and the future of the Muslim community.",
  "learningJourneySeerahHijrahSection1Title": "What hijrah required",
  "learningJourneySeerahHijrahSection1Body": "The migration to Madinah required planning, secrecy, courage, sacrifice, and complete reliance on Allah. It was not escape for comfort, but movement for faith.",
  "learningJourneySeerahHijrahSection2Title": "Trust and planning together",
  "learningJourneySeerahHijrahSection2Body": "Hijrah teaches that tawakkul is not passive. The Prophet ﷺ trusted Allah completely while still taking wise practical means.",
  "learningJourneySeerahHijrahBullet1": "Trust in Allah includes responsible action.",
  "learningJourneySeerahHijrahBullet2": "Leaving something for Allah can become a mercy.",
  "learningJourneySeerahHijrahBullet3": "Major transitions can open entirely new doors of good.",
  "learningJourneySeerahHijrahTakeaway1": "Hijrah joined courage with careful preparation.",
  "learningJourneySeerahHijrahTakeaway2": "Faithfulness sometimes requires hard transitions.",
  "learningJourneySeerahHijrahTakeaway3": "Tawakkul means trust plus effort.",
  "learningJourneySeerahHijrahReflection": "What important decision in your life needs both better planning and deeper trust in Allah?",
  "learningJourneySeerahMadinahTitle": "Madinah Society",
  "learningJourneySeerahMadinahIntro": "In Madinah, Islam was lived as worship, community, justice, brotherhood, and responsibility.",
  "learningJourneySeerahMadinahSection1Title": "What was built in Madinah",
  "learningJourneySeerahMadinahSection1Body": "The Prophet ﷺ established a masjid-centered community with worship, learning, brotherhood, agreements, teaching, family life, and leadership during peace and difficulty.",
  "learningJourneySeerahMadinahSection2Title": "Why this stage matters",
  "learningJourneySeerahMadinahSection2Body": "The Madinan period shows that Islam is not only personal belief. It also shapes society, relationships, public responsibility, and mutual care.",
  "learningJourneySeerahMadinahBullet1": "Islam builds individuals and community together.",
  "learningJourneySeerahMadinahBullet2": "The masjid is a center of worship, learning, and service.",
  "learningJourneySeerahMadinahBullet3": "Brotherhood and justice are part of lived faith.",
  "learningJourneySeerahMadinahTakeaway1": "Madinah shows Islam lived collectively, not privately alone.",
  "learningJourneySeerahMadinahTakeaway2": "Community life is part of Islamic growth.",
  "learningJourneySeerahMadinahTakeaway3": "Ibadah and public responsibility belong together.",
  "learningJourneySeerahMadinahReflection": "How can your worship become more connected to service, relationships, and community life?",
  "learningJourneySeerahLeadershipTitle": "Leadership and Character",
  "learningJourneySeerahLeadershipIntro": "The Prophet ﷺ led through mercy, truth, patience, courage, and concern for people.",
  "learningJourneySeerahLeadershipSection1Title": "What prophetic leadership looked like",
  "learningJourneySeerahLeadershipSection1Body": "He ﷺ listened, forgave, consulted, showed courage when needed, and remained gentle with people while firm on truth. His leadership never became self-promotion.",
  "learningJourneySeerahLeadershipSection2Title": "Character as leadership",
  "learningJourneySeerahLeadershipSection2Body": "Mercy, patience, and trustworthiness were not separate from his leadership. They were the very way he led.",
  "learningJourneySeerahLeadershipBullet1": "Mercy strengthens leadership rather than weakening it.",
  "learningJourneySeerahLeadershipBullet2": "Consultation and patience are prophetic habits.",
  "learningJourneySeerahLeadershipBullet3": "Character gives da‘wah its credibility.",
  "learningJourneySeerahLeadershipTakeaway1": "Prophetic leadership is worshipful, not ego-driven.",
  "learningJourneySeerahLeadershipTakeaway2": "Character and influence cannot be separated.",
  "learningJourneySeerahLeadershipTakeaway3": "Mercy and firmness both have their proper place.",
  "learningJourneySeerahLeadershipReflection": "Which prophetic quality would most improve the way you influence family, friends, or colleagues?",
  "learningJourneySeerahFinalSermonTitle": "Final Sermon",
  "learningJourneySeerahFinalSermonIntro": "The Farewell Sermon gathered major principles of dignity, justice, trust, and faithfulness near the end of the Prophet’s ﷺ mission.",
  "learningJourneySeerahFinalSermonSection1Title": "Key themes of the sermon",
  "learningJourneySeerahFinalSermonSection1Body": "The Prophet ﷺ emphasized the sanctity of life, wealth, and honor, the rights people owe one another, and the obligation to hold firmly to divine guidance.",
  "learningJourneySeerahFinalSermonSection2Title": "Why it remains urgent",
  "learningJourneySeerahFinalSermonSection2Body": "The Farewell Sermon gives a closing frame for the Seerah: worship Allah, honor people, protect trust, and remain faithful to revelation.",
  "learningJourneySeerahFinalSermonBullet1": "Human dignity and trust are sacred in Islam.",
  "learningJourneySeerahFinalSermonBullet2": "The Prophetic mission joined worship with justice and responsibility.",
  "learningJourneySeerahFinalSermonBullet3": "Guidance must remain central after the Prophet ﷺ has passed on.",
  "learningJourneySeerahFinalSermonTakeaway1": "The Final Sermon summarizes core prophetic values.",
  "learningJourneySeerahFinalSermonTakeaway2": "Justice and mercy are public Islamic responsibilities.",
  "learningJourneySeerahFinalSermonTakeaway3": "The Seerah ends by pointing believers back to revelation.",
  "learningJourneySeerahFinalSermonReflection": "Which principle from the Final Sermon feels most urgent for the time you live in?",
  "learningJourneyDhikrWhatIsTitle": "What Is Dhikr?",
  "learningJourneyDhikrWhatIsIntro": "Dhikr is remembering Allah with the heart, tongue, and life through praise, gratitude, repentance, and returning to Him often.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrWhatIsSection1Title": "A simple understanding",
  "learningJourneyDhikrWhatIsSection1Body": "Dhikr is not only repeating words. It is keeping Allah present in awareness through truthful phrases that soften the heart and direct the day.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrWhatIsSection2Title": "How to begin a habit",
  "learningJourneyDhikrWhatIsSection2Body": "Begin with a few short remembrances that you understand and can keep consistently. Small steady dhikr is better than overload that disappears.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrWhatIsBullet1": "Choose short authentic phrases first.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrWhatIsBullet2": "Attach remembrance to existing parts of your day.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrWhatIsBullet3": "Understanding meaning keeps dhikr sincere.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrWhatIsTakeaway1": "Dhikr is remembrance with meaning, not empty repetition.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrWhatIsTakeaway2": "Consistency matters more than size at the beginning.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrWhatIsTakeaway3": "The heart becomes calmer when Allah is remembered often.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrWhatIsReflection": "Which daily moment could most easily become a steady remembrance anchor for you?",
  "learningJourneyDhikrMorningTitle": "Morning Adhkar",
  "learningJourneyDhikrMorningIntro": "Morning adhkar begin the day with dependence on Allah, gratitude, and spiritual protection.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrMorningSection1Title": "When to say them",
  "learningJourneyDhikrMorningSection1Body": "Morning adhkar are best read after Fajr or in the early part of the day. A beginner can start with one or two authentic remembrances and keep them steady.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrMorningSection2Title": "Building the habit",
  "learningJourneyDhikrMorningSection2Body": "Keep the morning set small at first. Tie it to a clear moment such as after prayer, before leaving the house, or before opening your phone.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrMorningBullet1": "Begin with a short authentic opening remembrance.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrMorningBullet2": "Use the same moment each day so the habit becomes easier.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrMorningBullet3": "Read with understanding, not rush.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrMorningTakeaway1": "Morning adhkar set the tone of the day around Allah.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrMorningTakeaway2": "A short protected routine is better than an abandoned long list.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrMorningTakeaway3": "The day begins more calmly when remembrance comes before distraction.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrMorningReflection": "What would change in your mornings if remembrance came before hurry?",
  "learningJourneyDhikrMorningInvocationTitle": "Morning opening remembrance",
  "learningJourneyDhikrMorningInvocationMeaning": "O Allah, by You we enter the morning, by You we enter the evening, by You we live, by You we die, and to You is the resurrection.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrMorningInvocationContext": "Read in the morning to begin the day with trust in Allah.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrEveningTitle": "Evening Adhkar",
  "learningJourneyDhikrEveningIntro": "Evening adhkar close the day with reliance on Allah, gratitude, and calm before night.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrEveningSection1Title": "When to say them",
  "learningJourneyDhikrEveningSection1Body": "Evening adhkar are read after Asr or around sunset. They help the heart leave the noise of the day and return to Allah before sleep.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrEveningSection2Title": "How they help",
  "learningJourneyDhikrEveningSection2Body": "A short evening routine creates spiritual closure. It is a gentle way to end the day with remembrance instead of heaviness or heedlessness.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrEveningBullet1": "Choose one or two evening remembrances first.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrEveningBullet2": "Keep the routine light enough to survive tired days.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrEveningBullet3": "Treat the evening set as a return, not a burden.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrEveningTakeaway1": "Evening adhkar settle the heart before night.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrEveningTakeaway2": "A short evening habit can be built gradually.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrEveningTakeaway3": "Closing the day with dhikr changes how you carry its weight.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrEveningReflection": "What usually fills the end of your day, and how can remembrance reclaim part of it?",
  "learningJourneyDhikrEveningInvocationTitle": "Evening opening remembrance",
  "learningJourneyDhikrEveningInvocationMeaning": "O Allah, by You we enter the evening, by You we enter the morning, by You we live, by You we die, and to You is the final return.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrEveningInvocationContext": "Read in the evening to close the day with remembrance.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrAfterSalahTitle": "After Salah Dhikr",
  "learningJourneyDhikrAfterSalahIntro": "After each prayer, a simple set of adhkar helps protect the prayer and extend its effect into the rest of the day.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrAfterSalahSection1Title": "Why post-prayer dhikr matters",
  "learningJourneyDhikrAfterSalahSection1Body": "Because salah already gathers the heart, the moments after salam are one of the easiest places to build a stable dhikr habit.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrAfterSalahSection2Title": "How to keep it up",
  "learningJourneyDhikrAfterSalahSection2Body": "Start after one prayer each day if needed. Keep the rhythm calm and attentive instead of turning it into a rushed formula.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrAfterSalahBullet1": "Choose one prayer if all five feel too much at first.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrAfterSalahBullet2": "Understand the praise and glorification you are saying.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrAfterSalahBullet3": "Let the dhikr extend the calm of salah.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrAfterSalahTakeaway1": "Post-salah dhikr is one of the easiest daily anchors for remembrance.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrAfterSalahTakeaway2": "Short formulas can carry deep meaning when done with attention.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrAfterSalahTakeaway3": "Salah becomes more continuous when remembrance follows it.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrAfterSalahReflection": "Which prayer is the easiest place for you to begin a stable after-salah dhikr habit?",
  "learningJourneyDhikrAfterSalahInvocationTitle": "Post-prayer glorification",
  "learningJourneyDhikrAfterSalahInvocationMeaning": "Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, Allah is the Greatest.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrAfterSalahInvocationContext": "A simple dhikr set read after salah.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrRoutineTitle": "Simple Daily Routine",
  "learningJourneyDhikrRoutineIntro": "A beginner dhikr routine should be small, clear, and sustainable.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrRoutineSection1Title": "A workable routine",
  "learningJourneyDhikrRoutineSection1Body": "Choose three anchor moments: morning, after one prayer, and before sleep. Attach one short remembrance to each moment and keep it for a week before adding more.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrRoutineSection2Title": "What keeps the routine alive",
  "learningJourneyDhikrRoutineSection2Body": "Clarity matters more than intensity. A small routine that survives real life will benefit you more than a large routine that collapses quickly.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrRoutineBullet1": "Morning: one opening remembrance.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrRoutineBullet2": "After salah: one short fixed set.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrRoutineBullet3": "Night: one closing remembrance before sleep.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrRoutineTakeaway1": "Tie dhikr to moments that already exist in your day.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrRoutineTakeaway2": "Build slowly enough that the habit survives difficulty.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrRoutineTakeaway3": "Steady remembrance is formed by clarity, not pressure.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrRoutineReflection": "Which three moments could become your personal remembrance anchors this week?",
  "learningJourneyDhikrIstighfarTitle": "Istighfar",
  "learningJourneyDhikrIstighfarIntro": "Istighfar is seeking Allah’s forgiveness with humility, honesty, and hope in His mercy.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrIstighfarSection1Title": "Why istighfar matters daily",
  "learningJourneyDhikrIstighfarSection1Body": "A believer returns often to Allah, not only after major mistakes. Istighfar softens pride, cleans the heart, and keeps the servant close to mercy.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrIstighfarSection2Title": "How to build the habit",
  "learningJourneyDhikrIstighfarSection2Body": "Use istighfar after a sin, after heedlessness, after prayer, or whenever the heart feels dry and needs to return to Allah.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrIstighfarBullet1": "Repent quickly instead of delaying return.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrIstighfarBullet2": "Treat forgiveness as a daily need, not a rare emergency.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrIstighfarBullet3": "Say it with awareness of both weakness and hope.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrIstighfarTakeaway1": "Istighfar is a daily spiritual need.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrIstighfarTakeaway2": "Repentance joins honesty about sin with hope in mercy.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrIstighfarTakeaway3": "Short sincere repentance is better than thoughtless repetition.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrIstighfarReflection": "What would change if repentance became one of your daily habits instead of a rare reaction?",
  "learningJourneyDhikrIstighfarInvocationTitle": "Simple istighfar",
  "learningJourneyDhikrIstighfarInvocationMeaning": "I seek Allah’s forgiveness and I turn to Him in repentance.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrIstighfarInvocationContext": "A short daily formula of repentance and return.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrSalawatTitle": "Salawat",
  "learningJourneyDhikrSalawatIntro": "Sending prayers upon the Prophet ﷺ is an act of love, gratitude, and obedience to Allah.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrSalawatSection1Title": "Why salawat matters",
  "learningJourneyDhikrSalawatSection1Body": "Salawat keeps the heart connected to the Messenger ﷺ and reminds you that your path to Allah is shaped by following him with love and respect.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrSalawatSection2Title": "How to make it a habit",
  "learningJourneyDhikrSalawatSection2Body": "Use a short form daily, after hearing the Prophet’s ﷺ name, on Fridays, and in quiet moments to renew your love for his guidance.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrSalawatBullet1": "Keep a short form ready for frequent repetition.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrSalawatBullet2": "Let salawat renew love, not become empty habit.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrSalawatBullet3": "Use it often enough that gratitude becomes natural.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrSalawatTakeaway1": "Salawat grows love for the Prophet ﷺ in daily life.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrSalawatTakeaway2": "A short form used often is better than a long form rarely used.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrSalawatTakeaway3": "This remembrance connects worship to gratitude for guidance.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrSalawatReflection": "How can you make salawat part of your day in a way that feels sincere and frequent?",
  "learningJourneyDhikrSalawatInvocationTitle": "Short salawat",
  "learningJourneyDhikrSalawatInvocationMeaning": "O Allah, send prayers upon Muhammad.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrSalawatInvocationContext": "A short form for daily remembrance and frequent salawat.",
  "learningJourneyFaithBooksTitle": "Books",
  "learningJourneyFaithBooksIntro": "Allah sent books as guidance, mercy, and clarification for humanity.",
  "learningJourneyFaithBooksSection1Body": "Muslims believe Allah sent revelation to His messengers. Earlier scriptures were sent to earlier communities, and the Qur’an was sent as the final preserved guidance.",
  "learningJourneyFaithBooksSection2Body": "This belief teaches respect for revelation and gratitude for the Qur’an. It also reminds you that guidance is received humbly, not invented from desire.",
  "learningJourneyFaithBooksTakeaway1": "Allah guided people through revealed books.",
  "learningJourneyFaithBooksTakeaway2": "The Qur’an is the final preserved revelation.",
  "learningJourneyFaithBooksTakeaway3": "Belief in revelation teaches humility and gratitude.",
  "learningJourneyFaithBooksReflection": "How can you show more gratitude for having the Qur’an in your life?",
  "learningJourneyFaithProphetsTitle": "Prophets",
  "learningJourneyFaithProphetsIntro": "Allah sent prophets to guide people, clarify truth, and model faithful living.",
  "learningJourneyFaithProphetsSection1Body": "The prophets all called people to worship Allah alone. They differed in time and circumstance, but their message was one in its foundation.",
  "learningJourneyFaithProphetsSection2Body": "Learning about the prophets gives you examples of patience, courage, mercy, wisdom, and trust in Allah. Their lives make guidance feel real and lived.",
  "learningJourneyFaithProphetsTakeaway1": "The prophets shared one core message: worship Allah alone.",
  "learningJourneyFaithProphetsTakeaway2": "Their lives model patience and obedience.",
  "learningJourneyFaithProphetsTakeaway3": "Studying the prophets strengthens faith and hope.",
  "learningJourneyFaithProphetsReflection": "Which prophetic quality do you most want to imitate in your life right now?",
  "learningJourneyFaithJudgmentTitle": "Day of Judgment",
  "learningJourneyFaithJudgmentIntro": "The Day of Judgment reminds us that life has meaning, deeds matter, and every person will return to Allah.",
  "learningJourneyFaithJudgmentSection1Body": "Islam teaches that this world is not the final stop. Allah will resurrect creation, judge with perfect justice, and reward or punish with complete fairness.",
  "learningJourneyFaithJudgmentSection2Body": "Remembering the Hereafter can soften the heart, reduce arrogance, and make daily choices more sincere because you begin to live with accountability and hope.",
  "learningJourneyFaithJudgmentTakeaway1": "Life has accountability and purpose.",
  "learningJourneyFaithJudgmentTakeaway2": "Allah’s judgment is perfectly just.",
  "learningJourneyFaithJudgmentTakeaway3": "Remembering the Hereafter can improve daily choices.",
  "learningJourneyFaithJudgmentReflection": "What habit would you change first if you kept the Hereafter more clearly in mind?",
  "learningJourneyFaithQadrTitle": "Qadr",
  "learningJourneyFaithQadrIntro": "Qadr means Allah’s perfect knowledge, decree, and wisdom over what happens in creation.",
  "learningJourneyFaithQadrSection1Body": "Allah knows all things and nothing escapes His wisdom. Belief in qadr does not cancel responsibility. It teaches that you act sincerely while trusting what Allah allows to unfold.",
  "learningJourneyFaithQadrSection2Body": "This belief brings steadiness. In blessings, it protects from pride. In hardship, it protects from despair. You still strive, repent, and make dua while trusting Allah’s wisdom.",
  "learningJourneyFaithQadrTakeaway1": "Allah’s decree is wise and complete.",
  "learningJourneyFaithQadrTakeaway2": "Belief in qadr does not remove human responsibility.",
  "learningJourneyFaithQadrTakeaway3": "Qadr helps the heart stay balanced in ease and hardship.",
  "learningJourneyFaithQadrReflection": "Where do you need to combine personal effort with deeper trust in Allah’s wisdom?",
  "learningJourneyWordsTopTitle": "Open top Qur’anic words",
  "learningJourneyWordsTopIntro": "Recurring Qur’anic words are one of the fastest ways to increase familiarity and comprehension.",
  "learningJourneyWordsTopSection1Title": "Why recurring words help",
  "learningJourneyWordsTopSection1Body": "When you keep meeting the same words, the Qur’an starts feeling less distant. A small vocabulary can unlock many ayat more than people expect.",
  "learningJourneyWordsTopSection2Title": "How to begin well",
  "learningJourneyWordsTopSection2Body": "Choose a small cluster, repeat it often, and connect each word to one simple meaning instead of trying to collect too many terms at once.",
  "learningJourneyWordsTopBullet1": "Start with small repeated groups of words.",
  "learningJourneyWordsTopBullet2": "Use repetition to recognize words in real verses.",
  "learningJourneyWordsTopBullet3": "Let frequency guide what you learn first.",
  "learningJourneyWordsTopTakeaway1": "Recurring words create fast progress in comprehension.",
  "learningJourneyWordsTopTakeaway2": "Small focused sets are easier to retain.",
  "learningJourneyWordsTopTakeaway3": "Vocabulary should support real Qur’an reading, not remain isolated lists.",
  "learningJourneyWordsTopReflection": "What kind of word set would feel easiest for you to revisit consistently?",
  "learningJourneyWordsReviewTitle": "Review and retain",
  "learningJourneyWordsReviewIntro": "Vocabulary only becomes useful when it is reviewed often enough to stay active in memory.",
  "learningJourneyWordsReviewSection1Title": "Why review matters",
  "learningJourneyWordsReviewSection1Body": "Words fade quickly when they are only seen once. Review brings them back until recognition feels natural rather than forced.",
  "learningJourneyWordsReviewSection2Title": "A short memory loop",
  "learningJourneyWordsReviewSection2Body": "Use short frequent review sessions instead of long exhausting ones. Recognition grows through return and repetition.",
  "learningJourneyWordsReviewBullet1": "Review a little, but review often.",
  "learningJourneyWordsReviewBullet2": "Return to weak words before adding many new ones.",
  "learningJourneyWordsReviewBullet3": "Tie review to a moment you already use for learning.",
  "learningJourneyWordsReviewTakeaway1": "Retention grows through steady return.",
  "learningJourneyWordsReviewTakeaway2": "A calm review loop is better than overloaded memorization.",
  "learningJourneyWordsReviewTakeaway3": "Weak areas become easier when revisited without pressure.",
  "learningJourneyWordsReviewReflection": "Which review habit would make your Qur’anic vocabulary more stable this month?",
  "learningJourneyWordsPatternsTitle": "Patterns and meaning groups",
  "learningJourneyWordsPatternsIntro": "Words become easier to remember when you notice families, themes, and repeated meaning clusters instead of isolated entries.",
  "learningJourneyWordsPatternsSection1Title": "Grouping by meaning",
  "learningJourneyWordsPatternsSection1Body": "Try collecting words around worship, mercy, guidance, gratitude, or the Hereafter. Grouping by theme helps memory attach words to meaning.",
  "learningJourneyWordsPatternsSection2Title": "Reinforcement through patterns",
  "learningJourneyWordsPatternsSection2Body": "Notice when related words keep returning in similar contexts. That repetition is a memory tool, not an accident.",
  "learningJourneyWordsPatternsBullet1": "Group words by theme instead of only by list order.",
  "learningJourneyWordsPatternsBullet2": "Reconnect reviewed words to real verses when possible.",
  "learningJourneyWordsPatternsBullet3": "Use repeated patterns to reinforce memory gently.",
  "learningJourneyWordsPatternsTakeaway1": "Meaning groups make vocabulary easier to retain.",
  "learningJourneyWordsPatternsTakeaway2": "Patterns help the Qur’an feel more connected.",
  "learningJourneyWordsPatternsTakeaway3": "Memory grows when words are linked to themes and contexts.",
  "learningJourneyWordsPatternsReflection": "Which theme would you like to build a small Qur’anic word group around first?",
  "learningJourneyLessonSectionContinueWith": "Continue with",
  "learningJourneyLessonSectionRelatedJourneys": "Related journeys",
  "learningJourneyLessonSectionActionStep": "Small action step",
  "learningJourneyLessonSectionReviewSuggestion": "Review suggestion",
  "learningJourneyDetailCompletionTitle": "Journey complete",
  "learningJourneyDetailCompletionSubtitle": "You reached the end of this journey. Carry one thing into your day.",
  "learningJourneyDetailActionReviewJourney": "Review Journey",
  "learningJourneyBeautifulCharacterTitle": "Beautiful Character",
  "learningJourneyBeautifulCharacterSubtitle": "Grow through the qualities that beautify faith and daily life.",
  "learningJourneyBeautifulCharacterDescription": "Follow a guided journey through sincerity, patience, gratitude, humility, forgiveness, self-control, kindness, and final reflection.",
  "learningJourneyBeautifulCharacterOutcome1": "Understand core qualities of beautiful Islamic character",
  "learningJourneyBeautifulCharacterOutcome2": "Connect character to worship, relationships, and daily choices",
  "learningJourneyBeautifulCharacterOutcome3": "Leave with one clear next step for personal growth",
  "learningJourneyBeautifulCharacterWhyThisMatters": "Knowledge becomes lived Islam when it shapes character, speech, reactions, and service to others.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterIkhlasStageTitle": "Sincerity",
  "learningJourneyCharacterIkhlasStageSummary": "Begin with ikhlas so your actions are rooted in Allah alone.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterSabrStageTitle": "Patience",
  "learningJourneyCharacterSabrStageSummary": "Learn how sabr steadies faith through hardship, delay, and discipline.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterShukrStageTitle": "Gratitude",
  "learningJourneyCharacterShukrStageSummary": "See gratitude as worship of the heart, tongue, and daily choices.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterHumilityStageTitle": "Humility",
  "learningJourneyCharacterHumilityStageSummary": "Practice a humble heart while still standing firm on truth.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterForgivenessStageTitle": "Forgiveness",
  "learningJourneyCharacterForgivenessStageSummary": "Learn when forgiveness heals the heart and restores dignity.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterAngerStageTitle": "Controlling anger",
  "learningJourneyCharacterAngerStageSummary": "Train yourself to pause, restrain anger, and respond with wisdom.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterKindnessStageTitle": "Kindness",
  "learningJourneyCharacterKindnessStageSummary": "Carry mercy into speech, service, and everyday relationships.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterCompletionStageTitle": "Completion reflection",
  "learningJourneyCharacterCompletionStageSummary": "Gather what you learned and choose one character trait to keep practicing.",
  "learningJourneyWordsTopReviewSuggestion": "Review a small word set again tomorrow, then notice those words the next time you read Qur’an.",
  "learningJourneyWordsReviewSuggestion": "Use short, frequent review instead of long sessions so recognition stays light and steady.",
  "learningJourneyWordsPatternsActionStep": "Choose one small word family to notice in your next recitation or reading session.",
  "learningJourneyWordsPatternsReviewSuggestion": "Come back tomorrow and see whether the same meanings appear again in familiar verses.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomDailyQuoteTitle": "Receive one wise reminder",
  "learningJourneyWisdomDailyQuoteIntro": "A daily wisdom item should be small enough to carry and deep enough to reopen later in the day.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomDailyQuoteSection1Title": "What Daily Wisdom gathers",
  "learningJourneyWisdomDailyQuoteSection1Body": "Daily Wisdom brings short reminders from Qur’an, hadith, prophetic example, and reflection together, one at a time. The goal is not volume. The goal is one truthful reminder that stays with you.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomDailyQuoteSection2Title": "How to use one item well",
  "learningJourneyWisdomDailyQuoteSection2Body": "Read slowly, keep one idea, and let it shape one decision or dua before the day moves on.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomDailyQuoteBullet1": "Choose one line instead of trying to remember everything.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomDailyQuoteBullet2": "Return to it once later in the day.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomDailyQuoteBullet3": "Let it point you toward a deeper journey when you are ready.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomDailyQuoteTakeaway1": "One small reminder can be enough for a whole day.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomDailyQuoteTakeaway2": "Daily wisdom works best when it stays simple and consistent.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomDailyQuoteTakeaway3": "Short reminders should lead into deeper learning, not replace it.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomDailyQuoteReflection": "What reminder do you need today more than extra information?",
  "learningJourneyWisdomShortLessonTitle": "Turn wisdom into a short lesson",
  "learningJourneyWisdomShortLessonIntro": "A brief lesson helps a daily reminder grow roots. It explains just enough to make the reminder usable.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomShortLessonSection1Title": "Consistent explanation style",
  "learningJourneyWisdomShortLessonSection1Body": "Whether the source is a hadith, a verse, a prophetic event, or a reflection prompt, the explanation should stay calm, practical, and beginner-friendly. That keeps Daily Wisdom coherent.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomShortLessonSection2Title": "Where the lesson should lead",
  "learningJourneyWisdomShortLessonSection2Body": "A short lesson should end with a next step. That next step might be a journey, a tool, a short act of worship, or a practical decision.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomShortLessonBullet1": "Keep the explanation short enough to reread quickly.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomShortLessonBullet2": "Tie the reminder to daily life.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomShortLessonBullet3": "Offer one clear way to go deeper.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomShortLessonTakeaway1": "Good daily teaching is clear, not crowded.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomShortLessonTakeaway2": "A short lesson should help the heart and mind together.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomShortLessonTakeaway3": "Daily Wisdom should lead naturally into the wider journeys.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomShortLessonReflection": "Which kind of daily reminder opens you most: a verse, a hadith, a story, or a reflection question?",
  "learningJourneyWisdomPracticeTitle": "Carry wisdom into practice",
  "learningJourneyWisdomPracticeIntro": "The purpose of daily wisdom is not to collect quotes. It is to gently change speech, intention, habits, and attention.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomPracticeSection1Title": "One action is enough",
  "learningJourneyWisdomPracticeSection1Body": "Choose one small action that matches the reminder: pause before speaking, thank Allah aloud, forgive quickly, review one verse, or return to dhikr.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomPracticeSection2Title": "Build a repeatable rhythm",
  "learningJourneyWisdomPracticeSection2Body": "A stable rhythm might be: open one wisdom item, keep one sentence, act on one step, and revisit one related journey later.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomPracticeBullet1": "Do not overload the day with too many goals.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomPracticeBullet2": "Let repetition turn insight into habit.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomPracticeBullet3": "Use related journeys to go deeper.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomPracticeTakeaway1": "Wisdom becomes useful when it changes action.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomPracticeTakeaway2": "A small repeated act is stronger than a large short-lived intention.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomPracticeTakeaway3": "Daily Wisdom should send you back into your wider learning.",
  "learningJourneyWisdomPracticeReflection": "What is one small action you can do today so this reminder becomes lived knowledge?",
  "learningJourneyWisdomPracticeActionStep": "Before the day ends, return to this reminder once and ask whether it changed one choice, one word, or one dua.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterIkhlasTitle": "Sincerity (Ikhlas)",
  "learningJourneyCharacterIkhlasIntro": "Ikhlas means doing what is right for Allah, not for showing off, praise, or control.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterIkhlasSection1Title": "What sincerity does",
  "learningJourneyCharacterIkhlasSection1Body": "Sincerity purifies actions from the inside. Two people may do the same outward deed, but the one who seeks Allah alone carries a different weight with Him.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterIkhlasSection2Title": "How sincerity appears in real life",
  "learningJourneyCharacterIkhlasSection2Body": "Ikhlas shows up when you keep doing good even if no one notices, and when you correct your intention whenever pride tries to enter.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterIkhlasBullet1": "Renew your intention before a good deed.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterIkhlasBullet2": "Do some good privately when possible.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterIkhlasBullet3": "If praise reaches you, thank Allah and keep your heart steady.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterIkhlasTakeaway1": "Sincerity begins in the heart before it appears in action.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterIkhlasTakeaway2": "Private worship helps protect sincerity.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterIkhlasTakeaway3": "Ikhlas needs regular renewal, not a one-time decision.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterIkhlasReflection": "Which part of your worship or service needs a quieter intention?",
  "learningJourneyCharacterIkhlasActionStep": "Choose one small act today that only Allah knows you intended for Him.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterSabrTitle": "Patience (Sabr)",
  "learningJourneyCharacterSabrIntro": "Sabr is not passive weakness. It is steady obedience, self-restraint, and trust in Allah through difficulty.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterSabrSection1Title": "Where patience is needed",
  "learningJourneyCharacterSabrSection1Body": "Patience is needed in hardship, in delay, in resisting sin, and in staying consistent with worship when the heart feels low.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterSabrSection2Title": "A practical form of sabr",
  "learningJourneyCharacterSabrSection2Body": "Sabr often looks ordinary: lowering your reaction, continuing a duty, waiting without complaint, and asking Allah for help before speaking or acting.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterSabrBullet1": "Pause before reacting when frustrated.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterSabrBullet2": "Keep one obligation steady even on difficult days.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterSabrBullet3": "Ask Allah for help instead of collapsing into panic.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterSabrTakeaway1": "Patience is active strength, not passivity.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterSabrTakeaway2": "Sabr is needed in both hardship and obedience.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterSabrTakeaway3": "Short pauses can protect you from long regret.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterSabrReflection": "Where do you most need to slow down and trust Allah more?",
  "learningJourneyCharacterSabrActionStep": "The next time you feel pressure, pause, breathe, and delay your response for a few seconds.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterShukrTitle": "Gratitude (Shukr)",
  "learningJourneyCharacterShukrIntro": "Shukr means recognizing blessings from Allah and responding with praise, obedience, and better use of what He gave.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterShukrSection1Title": "Gratitude is more than words",
  "learningJourneyCharacterShukrSection1Body": "Saying Alhamdulillah matters, but gratitude also includes how you use time, health, wealth, knowledge, and relationships.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterShukrSection2Title": "How gratitude grows",
  "learningJourneyCharacterShukrSection2Body": "Gratitude grows when you notice specific blessings, name them, and turn them into worship and service instead of entitlement.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterShukrBullet1": "Name one blessing clearly instead of vaguely.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterShukrBullet2": "Use a blessing in a way Allah loves.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterShukrBullet3": "Do not let comfort make you forget the Giver.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterShukrTakeaway1": "Gratitude is a response of heart, tongue, and action.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterShukrTakeaway2": "Blessings become safer when they increase thankfulness.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterShukrTakeaway3": "Gratitude protects the heart from constant dissatisfaction.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterShukrReflection": "Which blessing have you become too used to noticing with gratitude?",
  "learningJourneyCharacterShukrActionStep": "Thank Allah specifically for one blessing today, then use it in one good way.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterHumilityTitle": "Humility",
  "learningJourneyCharacterHumilityIntro": "Humility means seeing your need for Allah clearly and treating people without arrogance.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterHumilitySection1Title": "Humility and truth",
  "learningJourneyCharacterHumilitySection1Body": "Humility does not mean weakness or self-erasure. It means accepting truth, lowering pride, and refusing to treat others with superiority.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterHumilitySection2Title": "How arrogance enters",
  "learningJourneyCharacterHumilitySection2Body": "Arrogance can hide inside knowledge, talent, worship, wealth, or social standing. Humility asks: do I still listen, learn, and respect others?",
  "learningJourneyCharacterHumilityBullet1": "Accept correction without defensiveness.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterHumilityBullet2": "Do not measure people only by status or outward polish.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterHumilityBullet3": "Remember that every gift is from Allah.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterHumilityTakeaway1": "Humility protects knowledge from becoming pride.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterHumilityTakeaway2": "A humble person can be firm without being arrogant.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterHumilityTakeaway3": "Remembering Allah reduces self-importance.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterHumilityReflection": "Where does pride make it harder for you to listen or change?",
  "learningJourneyCharacterHumilityActionStep": "Listen carefully to one person today without preparing your answer while they speak.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterForgivenessTitle": "Forgiveness",
  "learningJourneyCharacterForgivenessIntro": "Forgiveness softens the heart and frees it from carrying every injury forever.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterForgivenessSection1Title": "What forgiveness is and is not",
  "learningJourneyCharacterForgivenessSection1Body": "Forgiveness is not pretending harm was good. It is letting go of the desire to keep feeding resentment when forgiveness is wise and safe.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterForgivenessSection2Title": "Why forgiveness matters",
  "learningJourneyCharacterForgivenessSection2Body": "When a person forgives for Allah, the heart becomes lighter. Forgiveness can protect you from becoming shaped by the very harm you suffered.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterForgivenessBullet1": "Ask Allah to heal your heart before forcing yourself into words.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterForgivenessBullet2": "Keep justice and safety in view where needed.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterForgivenessBullet3": "Do not let resentment become your identity.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterForgivenessTakeaway1": "Forgiveness is strongest when done for Allah.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterForgivenessTakeaway2": "A soft heart can still keep wise boundaries.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterForgivenessTakeaway3": "Resentment harms the one carrying it.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterForgivenessReflection": "Is there one hurt you need to place before Allah so it stops ruling your heart?",
  "learningJourneyCharacterForgivenessActionStep": "Make dua for heart-healing before you think about how to respond to an old hurt.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterAngerTitle": "Controlling anger",
  "learningJourneyCharacterAngerIntro": "Anger itself may come, but Islamic character teaches restraint before anger becomes words or harm.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterAngerSection1Title": "Why anger needs discipline",
  "learningJourneyCharacterAngerSection1Body": "Anger narrows judgment quickly. A single uncontrolled moment can damage worship, relationships, and trust built over years.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterAngerSection2Title": "How to respond well",
  "learningJourneyCharacterAngerSection2Body": "Step back, lower your tone, seek refuge in Allah, change posture if needed, and avoid speaking while the heart is still inflamed.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterAngerBullet1": "Do not answer every irritation immediately.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterAngerBullet2": "Use silence before regretful words.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterAngerBullet3": "Return to dhikr to cool the heart.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterAngerTakeaway1": "Strength includes restraining yourself when angry.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterAngerTakeaway2": "Most anger mistakes happen in the first moments.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterAngerTakeaway3": "A calmer response protects dignity for everyone involved.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterAngerReflection": "What usually happens just before your anger becomes speech?",
  "learningJourneyCharacterAngerActionStep": "Choose one reset habit now: silence, changing posture, stepping away, or saying a short dhikr.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterKindnessTitle": "Kindness",
  "learningJourneyCharacterKindnessIntro": "Kindness is one of the clearest signs that knowledge has reached the heart.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterKindnessSection1Title": "Kindness in ordinary life",
  "learningJourneyCharacterKindnessSection1Body": "Kindness appears in small things: gentle speech, patient listening, thoughtful timing, service, smiling, and making room for others.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterKindnessSection2Title": "Why mercy matters",
  "learningJourneyCharacterKindnessSection2Body": "Mercy makes faith visible. People often feel Islam first through a Muslim’s character before they understand its deeper teachings.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterKindnessBullet1": "Make your speech softer without becoming unclear.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterKindnessBullet2": "Look for one hidden need you can ease today.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterKindnessBullet3": "Treat family and those closest to you with extra care.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterKindnessTakeaway1": "Kindness is one of the strongest forms of dawah in everyday life.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterKindnessTakeaway2": "Mercy belongs in speech, service, and correction.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterKindnessTakeaway3": "Gentleness often opens hearts that force cannot reach.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterKindnessReflection": "Who in your daily life most needs gentleness from you right now?",
  "learningJourneyCharacterKindnessActionStep": "Do one small act of gentleness today for someone who usually sees you in a rushed state.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterCompletionTitle": "Completion reflection",
  "learningJourneyCharacterCompletionIntro": "You have reached the end of this journey. Now the task is not more information. It is steady application.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterCompletionSection1Title": "Look back honestly",
  "learningJourneyCharacterCompletionSection1Body": "Which quality came easiest? Which one exposed your weakness? Honest reflection makes future growth real.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterCompletionSection2Title": "Choose one trait to carry",
  "learningJourneyCharacterCompletionSection2Body": "Do not try to perfect everything at once. Choose one quality that most needs attention in this season of life and keep returning to it.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterCompletionBullet1": "Choose one trait, not seven.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterCompletionBullet2": "Attach it to one daily situation.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterCompletionBullet3": "Revisit related journeys for reinforcement.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterCompletionTakeaway1": "Character grows by repetition, not intensity alone.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterCompletionTakeaway2": "Reflection helps you see where to begin again.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterCompletionTakeaway3": "The best completion is a small ongoing change.",
  "learningJourneyCharacterCompletionReflection": "Which single character trait will you keep working on over the next week?",
  "learningJourneyCharacterCompletionActionStep": "Write down one trait and one situation where you will consciously practice it this week.",
  "learningJourneyDhikrRoutineActionStep": "Choose one dhikr for the morning, one for the evening, and one after salah so your routine stays small and sustainable.",
  "learningJourneyHadithEssentialsTitle": "Hadith Essentials",
