  "learningJourneySalahFoundationsDescription": "Learn why salah matters, how to prepare for it, and how its words and movements work together.",
  "learningJourneySalahFoundationsOutcome1": "Understand why salah is central to a Muslim day",
  "learningJourneySalahFoundationsOutcome2": "Prepare for prayer with wudu, intention, and calm",
  "learningJourneySalahFoundationsOutcome3": "Connect movements, words, meaning, and consistency",
  "learningJourneySalahFoundationsWhyThisMatters": "Salah is a daily pillar, so even a small increase in clarity changes lived practice quickly.",
  "learningJourneyWuduJourneyTitle": "Journey of Wudu",
  "learningJourneyWuduJourneySubtitle": "Learn the order of wudu, its sunnah acts, and how to practice it.",
  "learningJourneyWuduJourneyDescription": "Move from understanding wudu to practicing it, checking what breaks it, and avoiding common mistakes.",
  "learningJourneyWuduJourneyOutcome1": "Understand why wudu matters before prayer",
  "learningJourneyWuduJourneyOutcome2": "Practice the sequence with confidence",
  "learningJourneyWuduJourneyOutcome3": "Recognize what breaks wudu and how to self-check calmly",
  "learningJourneyWuduJourneyWhyThisMatters": "Wudu is the daily gate into salah, so clarity here removes friction from worship.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanFoundationsTitle": "Ramadan Foundations",
  "learningJourneyRamadanFoundationsSubtitle": "A staged preparation path for fasting and Ramadan worship.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanFoundationsDescription": "Move through a simple beginner path that explains fasting, daily rhythm, spiritual goals, and common mistakes in Ramadan.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanFoundationsOutcome1": "Understand what Ramadan is and why Muslims fast",
  "learningJourneyRamadanFoundationsOutcome2": "Build a practical rhythm from suhoor to iftar",
  "learningJourneyRamadanFoundationsOutcome3": "Carry Ramadan with reflection, care, and spiritual goals",
  "learningJourneyRamadanFoundationsWhyThisMatters": "Ramadan is high impact and time-bound, so it benefits from a dedicated guided preparation path.",
  "learningJourneyArabicAlphabetTitle": "Arabic Alphabet Journey",
  "learningJourneyArabicAlphabetSubtitle": "Start with the letters and their sounds.",
  "learningJourneyArabicAlphabetDescription": "Learn the Arabic letters in calm groups, reinforce their sounds, and build a useful review habit before moving into reading.",
  "learningJourneyArabicAlphabetOutcome1": "Recognize the Arabic letters in manageable groups",
  "learningJourneyArabicAlphabetOutcome2": "Improve pronunciation through repetition",
  "learningJourneyArabicAlphabetOutcome3": "Build a review habit that prepares you for reading basics",
  "learningJourneyArabicAlphabetWhyThisMatters": "Letter confidence is the first real threshold into Qur’anic Arabic and reading.",
  "learningJourneyReadingBasicsTitle": "Reading Basics",
  "learningJourneyReadingBasicsSubtitle": "From letters to reading.",
  "learningJourneyReadingBasicsDescription": "Bridge the alphabet into harakat, joined letters, and calm reading checkpoints before wider recitation.",
  "learningJourneyReadingBasicsOutcome1": "Recognize the core reading marks and how they change sound",
  "learningJourneyReadingBasicsOutcome2": "Move from individual letters into joined reading",
  "learningJourneyReadingBasicsOutcome3": "Use review loops before advancing into wider recitation",
  "learningJourneyReadingBasicsWhyThisMatters": "Between learning the letters and reciting whole ayahs, most people need a middle step.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaPathsTitle": "Trivia Knowledge Paths",
  "learningJourneyTriviaPathsSubtitle": "Guided trivia paths that still teach in sequence.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaPathsDescription": "Use trivia as reinforcement with clear path selection, focused sessions, and guided follow-up into deeper journeys.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaPathsOutcome1": "Choose a trivia path with a learning purpose",
  "learningJourneyTriviaPathsOutcome2": "Use short sessions as reinforcement rather than isolated play",
  "learningJourneyTriviaPathsOutcome3": "Return from review into related journeys for depth",
  "learningJourneyTriviaPathsWhyThisMatters": "Well-staged trivia is an easy way into structured knowledge.",
  "learningJourneyStageHadithEssentialCollectionTitle": "Why hadith matters",
  "learningJourneyStageHadithEssentialCollectionSummary": "Begin with a simple frame for how hadith guides worship, character, and daily life.",
  "learningJourneyStageHadithThemesTitle": "Collections and themes",
  "learningJourneyStageHadithThemesSummary": "Learn how to begin with essential collections and then browse themes without overload.",
  "learningJourneyStageHadithReviewTitle": "Review and live the lesson",
  "learningJourneyStageHadithReviewSummary": "Use review as reinforcement and connect what you read to character and daily wisdom.",
  "learningJourneyStageSalahWhyTitle": "Why we pray",
  "learningJourneyStageSalahWhySummary": "Begin with the meaning of salah as a daily meeting with Allah and the anchor of worship.",
  "learningJourneyStageSalahPrepareTitle": "Prepare for prayer",
  "learningJourneyStageSalahPrepareSummary": "Learn how wudu, intention, timing, and calm prepare the heart and body for salah.",
  "learningJourneyStageSalahMovementsTitle": "Movements of salah",
  "learningJourneyStageSalahMovementsSummary": "Walk through the prayer posture by posture so the sequence feels calm and understandable.",
  "learningJourneyStageSalahWordsMeaningTitle": "What the words mean",
  "learningJourneyStageSalahWordsMeaningSummary": "Connect the words of salah to meaning so attention and khushu begin to grow together.",
  "learningJourneyStageSalahConsistencyTitle": "Consistency and khushu",
  "learningJourneyStageSalahConsistencySummary": "Finish by building a realistic rhythm for protecting prayer and returning after weak days.",
  "learningJourneyStageSalahCompletionTitle": "Carry salah forward",
  "learningJourneyStageSalahCompletionSummary": "Finish by choosing one concrete way to protect prayer, deepen focus, and continue learning.",
  "learningJourneyStageWuduWhyTitle": "Why wudu matters",
  "learningJourneyStageWuduWhySummary": "Begin with wudu as preparation, purification, and readiness for salah.",
  "learningJourneyStageWuduPracticeTitle": "Steps and practice",
  "learningJourneyStageWuduPracticeSummary": "Walk through the sequence calmly and use guided practice to stabilize the order.",
  "learningJourneyStageWuduBreaksTitle": "What breaks wudu",
  "learningJourneyStageWuduBreaksSummary": "Learn the common states that break wudu and how to stay calm instead of confused.",
  "learningJourneyStageWuduMistakesTitle": "Common mistakes and self-check",
  "learningJourneyStageWuduMistakesSummary": "Finish with practical reminders, confidence checks, and a gentle plan for improvement.",
  "learningJourneyStageWuduCompletionTitle": "Carry wudu into worship",
  "learningJourneyStageWuduCompletionSummary": "Finish by connecting confident wudu to calmer prayer preparation and steady worship.",
  "learningJourneyStageRamadanWhatIsTitle": "What is Ramadan",
  "learningJourneyStageRamadanWhatIsSummary": "Begin with what Ramadan is, why it is honored, and how it becomes a month of worship and mercy.",
  "learningJourneyStageRamadanWhyFastTitle": "Why we fast",
  "learningJourneyStageRamadanWhyFastSummary": "Learn the purpose of fasting and how it trains taqwa, gratitude, and restraint.",
  "learningJourneyStageRamadanSuhoorIftarTitle": "Suhoor and iftar",
  "learningJourneyStageRamadanSuhoorIftarSummary": "Build a practical daily rhythm from pre-dawn preparation to breaking the fast with gratitude.",
  "learningJourneyStageRamadanBreaksFastTitle": "What breaks the fast",
  "learningJourneyStageRamadanBreaksFastSummary": "Learn the common things that break the fast and how to avoid anxious uncertainty.",
  "learningJourneyStageRamadanLaylatTitle": "Laylat al-Qadr",
  "learningJourneyStageRamadanLaylatSummary": "Understand the weight of the last nights and how to seek Laylat al-Qadr with sincerity.",
  "learningJourneyStageRamadanSpiritualGoalsTitle": "Spiritual goals",
  "learningJourneyStageRamadanSpiritualGoalsSummary": "Set simple spiritual goals so Ramadan changes more than your meal schedule.",
  "learningJourneyStageRamadanMistakesTitle": "Common mistakes",
  "learningJourneyStageRamadanMistakesSummary": "Finish with practical reminders that protect fasting from confusion, burnout, and distraction.",
  "learningJourneyStageAlphabetOpenTitle": "Meet the letters",
  "learningJourneyStageAlphabetOpenSummary": "Start with calm letter groups so recognition feels manageable from the first session.",
  "learningJourneyStageAlphabetRepeatTitle": "Repeat and hear the sounds",
  "learningJourneyStageAlphabetRepeatSummary": "Use repetition and listening to make letter sounds steadier and easier to recall.",
  "learningJourneyStageAlphabetReviewTitle": "Review and prepare for reading",
  "learningJourneyStageAlphabetReviewSummary": "Use short review loops so the alphabet stays stable before you move into harakat and words.",
  "learningJourneyStageReadingFathahTitle": "Fathah",
  "learningJourneyStageReadingFathahSummary": "Begin reading with the short a sound and learn how it opens the mouth gently.",
  "learningJourneyStageReadingKasrahTitle": "Kasrah",
  "learningJourneyStageReadingKasrahSummary": "Learn the short i sound and how it changes the feel of a letter when reading.",
  "learningJourneyStageReadingDammahTitle": "Dammah",
  "learningJourneyStageReadingDammahSummary": "Practice the short u sound and notice how rounded reading stays calm and precise.",
  "learningJourneyStageReadingSukunTitle": "Sukun",
  "learningJourneyStageReadingSukunSummary": "Understand how a resting letter sounds when there is no vowel movement attached to it.",
  "learningJourneyStageReadingShaddahTitle": "Shaddah",
  "learningJourneyStageReadingShaddahSummary": "Learn how doubled letters sound and how to slow down enough to pronounce them clearly.",
  "learningJourneyStageReadingJoiningLettersTitle": "Joining letters",
  "learningJourneyStageReadingJoiningLettersSummary": "Move from single sounds into joined letters and short words without rushing.",
  "learningJourneyStageReadingCheckpointTitle": "Review and checkpoint",
  "learningJourneyStageReadingCheckpointSummary": "Pause, review, and notice which reading skill is ready and which one still needs another calm pass.",
  "learningJourneyStageTriviaPathsTitle": "Choose a knowledge path",
  "learningJourneyStageTriviaPathsSummary": "Begin by choosing a trivia path that matches a real learning goal, not just random questions.",
  "learningJourneyStageTriviaSessionTitle": "Use a short session well",
  "learningJourneyStageTriviaSessionSummary": "Treat each trivia round as focused reinforcement and pay attention to what you miss.",
  "learningJourneyStageTriviaReviewTitle": "Review and continue learning",
  "learningJourneyStageTriviaReviewSummary": "Use weak answers as signals for what to revisit, then continue into related real journeys.",
  "learningJourneyToolWuduGuideSubtitle": "Open the full wudu guide.",
  "learningJourneyToolWuduTrainerSubtitle": "Practice step by step.",
  "learningJourneyToolGuidedPrayerSubtitle": "Pray step by step with guidance.",
  "learningJourneyToolEssentialHadithSubtitle": "Start with the curated essentials.",
  "learningJourneyToolHadithHubSubtitle": "Hadith by theme and collection.",
  "learningJourneyToolHadithReviewSubtitle": "Revisit due or weak hadith material.",
  "learningJourneyToolDuaHubSubtitle": "Browse verified duas.",
  "learningJourneyToolTriviaPathsSubtitle": "Quizzes that build step by step.",
  "learningJourneyToolTriviaReviewSubtitle": "Review what is due next.",
  "learningJourneyHadithEssentialCollectionLessonIntro": "Hadith preserves the words, actions, and approvals of the Prophet ﷺ so Muslims can learn how revelation is lived.",
  "learningJourneyHadithEssentialCollectionSection1Title": "Why beginners need hadith",
  "learningJourneyHadithEssentialCollectionSection1Body": "The Qur’an gives guidance and command, and hadith shows how that guidance was embodied in prayer, character, mercy, and daily choices.",
  "learningJourneyHadithEssentialCollectionSection2Title": "How to start without overload",
  "learningJourneyHadithEssentialCollectionSection2Body": "Start with a small curated collection. Read slowly, keep one lesson, and let that lesson shape action before rushing into quantity.",
  "learningJourneyHadithEssentialCollectionBullet1": "Choose a trusted, beginner-safe collection.",
  "learningJourneyHadithEssentialCollectionBullet2": "Read for guidance, not for completion points.",
  "learningJourneyHadithEssentialCollectionBullet3": "Return to one hadith more than once before moving on.",
  "learningJourneyHadithEssentialCollectionTakeaway1": "Hadith explains how prophetic guidance becomes lived practice.",
  "learningJourneyHadithEssentialCollectionTakeaway2": "A small trusted starting point is enough for real growth.",
  "learningJourneyHadithEssentialCollectionTakeaway3": "Slow review is better than collecting texts without reflection.",
  "learningJourneyHadithEssentialCollectionReflection": "Which part of your daily life most needs prophetic guidance right now?",
  "learningJourneyHadithEssentialCollectionActionStep": "Open one essential hadith today and keep one sentence from it with you until evening.",
  "learningJourneyHadithThemesLessonIntro": "After a small essential set, themes help you learn hadith by need: worship, character, family life, repentance, and mercy.",
  "learningJourneyHadithThemesSection1Title": "Why themes help beginners",
  "learningJourneyHadithThemesSection1Body": "Themes gather related guidance together so learning feels practical. They help you see that hadith is not a random archive but a map for living.",
  "learningJourneyHadithThemesSection2Title": "How to use themed study well",
  "learningJourneyHadithThemesSection2Body": "Choose one theme for a few days. Read one hadith, understand its point, and ask how it should appear in your speech, worship, or relationships.",
  "learningJourneyHadithThemesBullet1": "Stay with one theme long enough to notice patterns.",
  "learningJourneyHadithThemesBullet2": "Do not jump topics every few minutes.",
  "learningJourneyHadithThemesBullet3": "Pair reading with one small change in behavior.",
  "learningJourneyHadithThemesTakeaway1": "Themes turn hadith study into a calmer guided path.",
  "learningJourneyHadithThemesTakeaway2": "One theme lived well is better than many themes skimmed quickly.",
  "learningJourneyHadithThemesTakeaway3": "Hadith learning should move from text to conduct.",
  "learningJourneyHadithThemesReflection": "Which theme would most help your life this week: worship, character, family, or repentance?",
  "learningJourneyHadithThemesReviewSuggestion": "After reading a theme, return the next day and ask what you still remember without reopening the page.",
  "learningJourneyHadithReviewLessonIntro": "Review keeps hadith from remaining inspirational for one moment and forgotten the next. It helps guidance become memory and habit.",
  "learningJourneyHadithReviewSection1Title": "What review protects",
  "learningJourneyHadithReviewSection1Body": "Without review, useful hadith fades quickly. A short return visit helps you notice what stuck, what blurred, and what still needs explanation.",
  "learningJourneyHadithReviewSection2Title": "How to review with purpose",
  "learningJourneyHadithReviewSection2Body": "Review is not only about right answers. It is about asking whether the hadith changed your choices, speech, or attention after you first read it.",
  "learningJourneyHadithReviewBullet1": "Revisit weak or forgotten items first.",
  "learningJourneyHadithReviewBullet2": "Link each hadith to one practical action.",
  "learningJourneyHadithReviewBullet3": "Let review send you back into deeper journeys.",
  "learningJourneyHadithReviewTakeaway1": "Review turns short exposure into steady knowledge.",
  "learningJourneyHadithReviewTakeaway2": "Weak spots show where more reflection is needed.",
  "learningJourneyHadithReviewTakeaway3": "The best review ends in better character, not just recall.",
  "learningJourneyHadithReviewReflection": "Which hadith lesson do you need to revisit until it becomes part of your conduct?",
  "learningJourneyHadithReviewActionStep": "Choose one hadith you reviewed and write down one thing it should change.",
  "learningJourneySalahWhyLessonIntro": "Salah is not only a duty on a list. It is the daily act that reorders the heart, brings the servant back to Allah, and gives the day structure.",
  "learningJourneySalahWhySection1Title": "What salah gives the believer",
  "learningJourneySalahWhySection1Body": "Salah gathers remembrance, humility, recitation, gratitude, and need before Allah. It keeps the day from becoming fully controlled by distraction or impulse.",
  "learningJourneySalahWhySection2Title": "A beginner way to think about prayer",
  "learningJourneySalahWhySection2Body": "Start by seeing salah as a return, not a performance. Each prayer is another chance to stand before Allah with honesty, even after weak days.",
  "learningJourneySalahWhyBullet1": "Salah reconnects the day to Allah.",
  "learningJourneySalahWhyBullet2": "It is a return even when you do not feel perfect.",
  "learningJourneySalahWhyBullet3": "Consistency matters more than emotional intensity.",
  "learningJourneySalahWhyTakeaway1": "Salah is an anchor, not an interruption.",
  "learningJourneySalahWhyTakeaway2": "Salah gathers the heart around remembrance and obedience.",
  "learningJourneySalahWhyTakeaway3": "A sincere return is always better than delay through guilt.",
  "learningJourneySalahWhyReflection": "What usually makes prayer feel heavy, and how would it change if you saw it as a return?",
  "learningJourneySalahPrepareLessonIntro": "Preparation shapes the quality of salah. Wudu, intention, timing, and a little calm make prayer more focused before the first takbir.",
  "learningJourneySalahPrepareSection1Title": "Prepare the body and heart",
  "learningJourneySalahPrepareSection1Body": "Wudu cleans and settles you. Clear intention reminds you who the prayer is for. Reaching prayer in time gives your heart more room to arrive before your tongue begins.",
  "learningJourneySalahPrepareSection2Title": "Keep preparation simple and repeatable",
  "learningJourneySalahPrepareSection2Body": "You do not need a perfect atmosphere every time. You need a few reliable habits that help you arrive with care.",
  "learningJourneySalahPrepareBullet1": "Renew wudu with attention.",
  "learningJourneySalahPrepareBullet2": "Pause briefly before takbir.",
  "learningJourneySalahPrepareBullet3": "Let prayer time shape your schedule instead of always reacting late.",
  "learningJourneySalahPrepareTakeaway1": "Good preparation makes prayer gentler.",
  "learningJourneySalahPrepareTakeaway2": "Wudu and intention are part of the path into salah.",
  "learningJourneySalahPrepareTakeaway3": "A small pause before prayer can change its whole feel.",
  "learningJourneySalahPrepareReflection": "Which part of preparing for prayer would most improve your focus right now?",
  "learningJourneySalahMovementsLessonIntro": "The movements of salah are not empty motions. Each posture carries meaning: standing, bowing, prostrating, and sitting before Allah.",
  "learningJourneySalahMovementsSection1Title": "Follow the sequence",
  "learningJourneySalahMovementsSection1Body": "Salah becomes easier when you stop trying to rush through the whole unit at once. Learn the sequence one posture at a time and connect each movement to its purpose.",
  "learningJourneySalahMovementsSection2Title": "What the postures teach",
  "learningJourneySalahMovementsSection2Body": "Standing teaches attention, bowing teaches humility, and sujud teaches nearness and surrender. The body helps train the heart.",
  "learningJourneySalahMovementsBullet1": "Slow down enough to recognize each posture.",
  "learningJourneySalahMovementsBullet2": "Link movement to meaning.",
  "learningJourneySalahMovementsBullet3": "Use guided practice when the order still feels unstable.",
  "learningJourneySalahMovementsTakeaway1": "The sequence becomes lighter with calm repetition.",
  "learningJourneySalahMovementsTakeaway2": "Each posture trains humility in a different way.",
  "learningJourneySalahMovementsTakeaway3": "Learning prayer is easier when you break it into parts.",
  "learningJourneySalahMovementsReflection": "Which posture in salah feels least familiar or least meaningful to you right now?",
  "learningJourneySalahWordsMeaningLessonIntro": "The words of salah become more powerful when you know what you are saying and why those words were placed in prayer.",
  "learningJourneySalahWordsMeaningSection1Title": "Meaning helps khushu",
  "learningJourneySalahWordsMeaningSection1Body": "Understanding Al-Fatihah, takbir, tasbih, and simple remembrances gives the heart something to hold during prayer. Meaning does not replace concentration, but it helps awaken it.",
  "learningJourneySalahWordsMeaningSection2Title": "Start with the most repeated phrases",
  "learningJourneySalahWordsMeaningSection2Body": "You do not need to understand everything at once. Begin with the phrases you recite every day and let familiarity grow into attention.",
  "learningJourneySalahWordsMeaningBullet1": "Start with Al-Fatihah and takbir.",
  "learningJourneySalahWordsMeaningBullet2": "Notice what you say in ruku and sujud.",
  "learningJourneySalahWordsMeaningBullet3": "Use repetition to deepen meaning, not flatten it.",
  "learningJourneySalahWordsMeaningTakeaway1": "Meaning helps the heart stay present.",
  "learningJourneySalahWordsMeaningTakeaway2": "A few understood phrases can change the quality of prayer quickly.",
  "learningJourneySalahWordsMeaningTakeaway3": "Understanding grows best in small repeated steps.",
  "learningJourneySalahWordsMeaningReflection": "Which phrase in salah do you most want to understand more deeply?",
  "learningJourneySalahConsistencyLessonIntro": "Consistency in salah is built through return, not through waiting to feel perfect. Khushu also grows gradually through repetition, understanding, and honest effort.",
  "learningJourneySalahConsistencySection1Title": "Protect the habit",
  "learningJourneySalahConsistencySection1Body": "A protected prayer habit often begins with one or two strong anchors, then expands. Even after weak days, the answer is return, not self-abandonment.",
  "learningJourneySalahConsistencySection2Title": "Build focus over time",
  "learningJourneySalahConsistencySection2Body": "Khushu is helped by preparation, understanding, and lowering distraction before prayer. It is not all-or-nothing.",
  "learningJourneySalahConsistencyBullet1": "Return quickly after a weak day.",
  "learningJourneySalahConsistencyBullet2": "Keep one prayer especially guarded if all five feel shaky.",
  "learningJourneySalahConsistencyBullet3": "Reduce one distraction before each prayer.",
  "learningJourneySalahConsistencyTakeaway1": "Consistency grows through quick return.",
  "learningJourneySalahConsistencyTakeaway2": "Khushu is built, not instantly achieved.",
  "learningJourneySalahConsistencyTakeaway3": "A small protected routine is stronger than grand temporary effort.",
  "learningJourneySalahConsistencyReflection": "What one change would help you protect salah more consistently this week?",
  "learningJourneySalahConsistencyActionStep": "Choose one prayer today to guard with extra care, from preparation to final salam.",
  "learningJourneySalahCompletionLessonIntro": "You have moved through the meaning, preparation, movements, and consistency of salah. Now choose how to keep prayer alive beyond this journey.",
  "learningJourneySalahCompletionSection1Title": "What this journey gave you",
  "learningJourneySalahCompletionSection1Body": "You now have a calmer frame for why salah matters, how to prepare for it, and how meaning and focus can grow together in prayer.",
  "learningJourneySalahCompletionSection2Title": "What to do next",
  "learningJourneySalahCompletionSection2Body": "Protect one concrete next step: steadier timing, better preparation, more presence in Al-Fatihah, or a stronger return after weak days.",
  "learningJourneySalahCompletionBullet1": "Choose one prayer habit to protect first.",
  "learningJourneySalahCompletionBullet2": "Use wudu and meaning journeys as reinforcement.",
  "learningJourneySalahCompletionBullet3": "Return quickly after weak days instead of delaying.",
  "learningJourneySalahCompletionTakeaway1": "Salah grows through steady return.",
  "learningJourneySalahCompletionTakeaway2": "Meaning, preparation, and focus belong together.",
  "learningJourneySalahCompletionTakeaway3": "One protected habit can change the whole prayer day.",
  "learningJourneySalahCompletionReflection": "Which one part of salah most deserves focused care from you this week?",
  "learningJourneySalahCompletionActionStep": "Choose one specific prayer improvement for this week and keep it small enough to stay consistent.",
  "learningJourneyWuduWhyLessonIntro": "Wudu prepares the believer to stand before Allah with cleanliness, readiness, and respect.",
  "learningJourneyWuduWhySection1Title": "More than washing",
  "learningJourneyWuduWhySection1Body": "Wudu is physical preparation, but it also slows the body down and signals that prayer is approaching. It helps you enter worship with a clear niyyah.",
  "learningJourneyWuduWhySection2Title": "A frame for beginners",
  "learningJourneyWuduWhySection2Body": "Think of wudu as a regular doorway into salah. When the doorway becomes familiar, worship feels less heavy.",
  "learningJourneyWuduWhyBullet1": "Wudu prepares you for prayer, not only cleanliness.",
  "learningJourneyWuduWhyBullet2": "Regular repetition makes the sequence easier.",
  "learningJourneyWuduWhyBullet3": "Clarity in wudu reduces stress before salah.",
  "learningJourneyWuduWhyTakeaway1": "Wudu is preparation with purpose.",
  "learningJourneyWuduWhyTakeaway2": "A familiar doorway makes prayer easier to enter.",
  "learningJourneyWuduWhyTakeaway3": "Small confidence in wudu removes worship friction.",
  "learningJourneyWuduWhyReflection": "What part of wudu still feels uncertain enough to slow you down before prayer?",
  "learningJourneyWuduPracticeLessonIntro": "The wudu sequence becomes stable when you practice it step by step instead of trying to hold everything in your head at once.",
  "learningJourneyWuduPracticeSection1Title": "Learn the order",
  "learningJourneyWuduPracticeSection1Body": "Move through the acts in order and let repetition make the pattern familiar. Calm practice is more useful than anxious speed.",
  "learningJourneyWuduPracticeSection2Title": "Use the trainer well",
  "learningJourneyWuduPracticeSection2Body": "A trainer helps when you need visual repetition or a guided pass through the steps. It is there to support memory, not replace attention.",
  "learningJourneyWuduPracticeBullet1": "Practice one clear pass at a time.",
  "learningJourneyWuduPracticeBullet2": "Repeat the order until it feels natural.",
  "learningJourneyWuduPracticeBullet3": "Use guided support when confusion returns.",
  "learningJourneyWuduPracticeTakeaway1": "Order becomes easier through repetition.",
  "learningJourneyWuduPracticeTakeaway2": "Guided practice lowers uncertainty.",
  "learningJourneyWuduPracticeTakeaway3": "You do not need to rush to build confidence.",
  "learningJourneyWuduPracticeReflection": "Which step in the sequence do you still mentally check twice?",
  "learningJourneyWuduBreaksLessonIntro": "Knowing what breaks wudu protects you from both carelessness and unnecessary anxiety.",
  "learningJourneyWuduBreaksSection1Title": "Learn the common cases first",
  "learningJourneyWuduBreaksSection1Body": "Start with the most common situations that clearly break wudu. Beginners do not need to begin with rare edge cases.",
  "learningJourneyWuduBreaksSection2Title": "Avoid anxious overchecking",
  "learningJourneyWuduBreaksSection2Body": "Islam is not asking you to live in suspicion. Learn the clear cases and do not let whispering turn worship into constant uncertainty.",
  "learningJourneyWuduBreaksBullet1": "Focus on clear common cases first.",
  "learningJourneyWuduBreaksBullet2": "Do not keep reopening doubtful situations without reason.",
  "learningJourneyWuduBreaksBullet3": "Ask for clarity when a real confusion remains.",
  "learningJourneyWuduBreaksTakeaway1": "Clarity protects worship from anxiety.",
  "learningJourneyWuduBreaksTakeaway2": "Beginners should learn the clear cases first.",
  "learningJourneyWuduBreaksTakeaway3": "Not every doubt deserves equal attention.",
  "learningJourneyWuduBreaksReflection": "Do you tend to struggle more with not knowing the rule or with overthinking it?",
  "learningJourneyWuduMistakesLessonIntro": "Confidence in wudu grows when you notice a few common mistakes and learn how to correct them without harshness.",
  "learningJourneyWuduMistakesSection1Title": "Common mistakes",
  "learningJourneyWuduMistakesSection1Body": "People often rush the order, skip attention, or let uncertainty keep them repeating more than needed. Calm correction is better than constant restarting.",
  "learningJourneyWuduMistakesSection2Title": "A simple self-check",
  "learningJourneyWuduMistakesSection2Body": "Ask yourself whether you know the sequence, can complete it without panic, and know when to repeat a step and when to move on.",
  "learningJourneyWuduMistakesBullet1": "Slow down before restarting everything.",
  "learningJourneyWuduMistakesBullet2": "Review the sequence after mistakes instead of only feeling frustrated.",
  "learningJourneyWuduMistakesBullet3": "Use practice to remove one weak point at a time.",
  "learningJourneyWuduMistakesTakeaway1": "Mistakes are corrected through calm review.",
  "learningJourneyWuduMistakesTakeaway2": "Confidence comes from clarity, not from repeating endlessly.",
  "learningJourneyWuduMistakesTakeaway3": "Self-check should support worship, not burden it.",
  "learningJourneyWuduMistakesReflection": "Which one weak point in wudu would be most useful to fix this week?",
  "learningJourneyWuduMistakesActionStep": "Practice one full calm pass of wudu today and note only one step that still needs attention.",
  "learningJourneyWuduCompletionLessonIntro": "You have moved from understanding wudu to practice, clarity, and self-check. Now connect that confidence to calmer worship.",
  "learningJourneyWuduCompletionSection1Title": "What this journey built",
  "learningJourneyWuduCompletionSection1Body": "You now know why wudu matters, how to practice it, what breaks it, and how to correct common mistakes without panic.",
  "learningJourneyWuduCompletionSection2Title": "What to do next",
  "learningJourneyWuduCompletionSection2Body": "Let confident wudu reduce friction before salah. Treat it as the doorway to prayer, dhikr, and steadier worship instead of a repeated source of stress.",
  "learningJourneyWuduCompletionBullet1": "Keep one calm full wudu routine alive.",
  "learningJourneyWuduCompletionBullet2": "Use what you learned before each prayer.",
  "learningJourneyWuduCompletionBullet3": "Let wudu support calmer entry into salah and dhikr.",
  "learningJourneyWuduCompletionTakeaway1": "Clarity in wudu supports clarity in worship.",
  "learningJourneyWuduCompletionTakeaway2": "Confidence grows through repetition and calm correction.",
  "learningJourneyWuduCompletionTakeaway3": "The goal is worship readiness, not anxious perfection.",
  "learningJourneyWuduCompletionReflection": "How would your prayer life change if wudu felt calm and familiar every day?",
  "learningJourneyWuduCompletionActionStep": "Before your next prayer, complete wudu slowly and notice how that changes your entry into salah.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetOpenLessonIntro": "The Arabic alphabet becomes easier when you stop seeing it as one large wall and begin meeting the letters in small memorable groups.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetOpenSection1Title": "Focus of this stage",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetOpenSection1Body": "Notice the broad shapes of the letters and how groups of letters can be learned together. The goal is recognition first, not perfect pronunciation in one sitting.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetOpenSection2Title": "Simple examples and next step",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetOpenSection2Body": "Work through a few letters, say their names out loud, and point out which shapes feel similar or different. That keeps your eyes active and your memory engaged.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetOpenBullet1": "Learn a small letter group at a time.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetOpenBullet2": "Say each letter aloud as you see it.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetOpenBullet3": "Notice one feature that helps you remember the shape.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetOpenTakeaway1": "Recognition comes before speed.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetOpenTakeaway2": "Small groups are easier to retain than the whole alphabet at once.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetOpenTakeaway3": "Active noticing makes letters stick better.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetOpenReflection": "Which letter shapes already feel familiar, and which ones still blur together?",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetRepeatLessonIntro": "Repetition turns alphabet exposure into alphabet memory. Hearing and repeating the sounds helps the letters settle more deeply.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetRepeatSection1Title": "What you are strengthening",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetRepeatSection1Body": "This stage is about sound recognition and steady repetition. When your tongue and ear work together, letter recall improves.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetRepeatSection2Title": "How to repeat well",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetRepeatSection2Body": "Repeat a short group several times instead of jumping quickly through everything. Slow repetition is more useful than tired repetition.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetRepeatBullet1": "Repeat one small group until it feels lighter.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetRepeatBullet2": "Listen carefully before copying the sound.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetRepeatBullet3": "Return to difficult letters more often.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetRepeatTakeaway1": "Hearing and speaking reinforce each other.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetRepeatTakeaway2": "Short focused repetition works better than random drilling.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetRepeatTakeaway3": "The hardest letters need gentler extra review, not frustration.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetRepeatReflection": "Which sound still feels least stable when you say it aloud?",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetReviewLessonIntro": "Review prepares you for reading. The alphabet becomes useful when you can return to it easily without feeling lost.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetReviewSection1Title": "Use review as reinforcement",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetReviewSection1Body": "A quick review loop helps you notice which letters stayed clear and which ones still need another pass before reading marks are added.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetReviewSection2Title": "Prepare for the next journey",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetReviewSection2Body": "Once the letters feel familiar, you are ready to start reading marks and joined forms. You do not need perfection. You need workable confidence.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetReviewBullet1": "Return to weak letters on purpose.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetReviewBullet2": "Check whether you can recognize letters out of order.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetReviewBullet3": "Move into reading basics once recognition feels workable.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetReviewTakeaway1": "Review turns exposure into readiness.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetReviewTakeaway2": "You can move forward with workable confidence, not perfection.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetReviewTakeaway3": "Preparation makes the next journey less intimidating.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetReviewReflection": "Are you more ready to move on, or do you need one more calm alphabet pass?",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetReviewActionStep": "Open one short alphabet review session and note the two letters you want to remember best this week.",
  "learningJourneyReadingKasrahLessonIntro": "Kasrah gives a short i sound. This small mark changes the feel of a letter and is one of the first keys to real reading.",
  "learningJourneyReadingKasrahSection1Title": "What to watch for",
  "learningJourneyReadingKasrahSection1Body": "Look beneath the letter and let your eye catch the mark before your tongue moves. That pause helps prevent guessing.",
  "learningJourneyReadingKasrahSection2Title": "Practice suggestion",
  "learningJourneyReadingKasrahSection2Body": "Read short examples with one letter at a time, then repeat two or three examples until the pattern begins to feel natural.",
  "learningJourneyReadingKasrahBullet1": "Notice the mark before saying the sound.",
  "learningJourneyReadingKasrahBullet2": "Use short repeated examples.",
  "learningJourneyReadingKasrahBullet3": "Do not rush from recognition into speed.",
  "learningJourneyReadingKasrahTakeaway1": "Kasrah trains careful seeing.",
  "learningJourneyReadingKasrahTakeaway2": "Short repetition stabilizes the sound.",
  "learningJourneyReadingKasrahTakeaway3": "Accuracy now makes later reading smoother.",
  "learningJourneyReadingKasrahReflection": "Does kasrah feel different from fathah in your mouth and attention yet?",
  "learningJourneyReadingDammahLessonIntro": "Dammah gives a short u sound and teaches the reader to stay calm with rounded pronunciation.",
  "learningJourneyReadingDammahSection1Title": "What the mark changes",
  "learningJourneyReadingDammahSection1Body": "The sound rounds differently from fathah and kasrah. Noticing that difference helps you stop treating all marks as the same.",
  "learningJourneyReadingDammahSection2Title": "Practice suggestion",
  "learningJourneyReadingDammahSection2Body": "Alternate between a few examples of the three short vowels so your ear and tongue learn to separate them clearly.",
  "learningJourneyReadingDammahBullet1": "Compare it with the other short vowels.",
  "learningJourneyReadingDammahBullet2": "Read slowly enough to hear the rounding.",
  "learningJourneyReadingDammahBullet3": "Repeat until the sound feels distinct.",
  "learningJourneyReadingDammahTakeaway1": "Each vowel mark deserves its own attention.",
  "learningJourneyReadingDammahTakeaway2": "Comparison helps memory.",
  "learningJourneyReadingDammahTakeaway3": "Rounded reading still needs calm precision.",
  "learningJourneyReadingDammahReflection": "Which short vowel still feels easiest to mix up with another one?",
  "learningJourneyReadingSukunLessonIntro": "Sukun teaches you what happens when a letter rests without a vowel. That resting sound is important for clearer reading.",
  "learningJourneyReadingSukunSection1Title": "How sukun feels",
  "learningJourneyReadingSukunSection1Body": "A letter with sukun does not carry a new vowel movement. Instead, you stop on the letter and hear its rest clearly.",
  "learningJourneyReadingSukunSection2Title": "Practice suggestion",
  "learningJourneyReadingSukunSection2Body": "Use simple examples where the contrast between a moving letter and a resting letter is easy to hear.",
  "learningJourneyReadingSukunBullet1": "Notice the difference between movement and rest.",
  "learningJourneyReadingSukunBullet2": "Pause enough to hear the resting letter.",
  "learningJourneyReadingSukunBullet3": "Use simple examples before longer words.",
  "learningJourneyReadingSukunTakeaway1": "Sukun teaches stillness in reading.",
  "learningJourneyReadingSukunTakeaway2": "Resting letters help words sound correct.",
  "learningJourneyReadingSukunTakeaway3": "Small listening differences matter.",
  "learningJourneyReadingSukunReflection": "Do resting letters still make you want to add a vowel automatically?",
  "learningJourneyReadingShaddahLessonIntro": "Shaddah shows a doubled sound. It asks you to slow down enough to hear and pronounce the letter with more care.",
  "learningJourneyReadingShaddahSection1Title": "Why shaddah matters",
  "learningJourneyReadingShaddahSection1Body": "A doubled letter changes how a word sounds. Missing it can flatten the word and make recitation less precise.",
  "learningJourneyReadingShaddahSection2Title": "Practice suggestion",
  "learningJourneyReadingShaddahSection2Body": "Use short words and exaggerate the doubled sound slightly at first. Once the pattern is clear, soften into normal reading.",
  "learningJourneyReadingShaddahBullet1": "Slow down at the doubled letter.",
  "learningJourneyReadingShaddahBullet2": "Use short words before longer lines.",
  "learningJourneyReadingShaddahBullet3": "Listen for the difference between one sound and two.",
  "learningJourneyReadingShaddahTakeaway1": "Shaddah rewards slower reading.",
  "learningJourneyReadingShaddahTakeaway2": "Pronunciation improves when the doubled sound is respected.",
  "learningJourneyReadingShaddahTakeaway3": "Small sound details matter in recitation.",
  "learningJourneyReadingShaddahReflection": "Does slowing down at a doubled letter make reading feel calmer or heavier for you right now?",
  "learningJourneyTriviaPathsLessonIntro": "Trivia works best when it supports a learning goal. A path gives your questions context and helps reinforcement feel purposeful.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaPathsSection1Title": "Why paths matter",
  "learningJourneyTriviaPathsSection1Body": "A themed path keeps questions connected. That makes it easier to remember what you learned and to continue into a deeper journey later.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaPathsSection2Title": "How to choose well",
  "learningJourneyTriviaPathsSection2Body": "Choose a path that matches something you are already studying or something you genuinely want to understand better.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaPathsBullet1": "Choose one path instead of random jumping.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaPathsBullet2": "Let curiosity and current study guide your choice.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaPathsBullet3": "Use paths as a way into deeper learning.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaPathsTakeaway1": "Trivia is stronger when it has a clear theme.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaPathsTakeaway2": "Connected questions are easier to retain.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaPathsTakeaway3": "A good path should point beyond the quiz itself.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaPathsReflection": "Which area would you rather reinforce right now: Prophets, Qur’an, worship, or history?",
  "learningJourneyTriviaSessionLessonIntro": "A short trivia session can reinforce knowledge well if you use it as learning, not only as scoring.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaSessionSection1Title": "How to answer well",
  "learningJourneyTriviaSessionSection1Body": "Slow down before guessing. Let each question teach you something, especially when you miss it.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaSessionSection2Title": "How to learn from mistakes",
  "learningJourneyTriviaSessionSection2Body": "A missed answer is a clue. It shows you which topic needs another pass through a real lesson or journey.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaSessionBullet1": "Treat mistakes as direction, not embarrassment.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaSessionBullet2": "Pause after wrong answers long enough to notice the lesson.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaSessionBullet3": "Return to related journeys after the session.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaSessionTakeaway1": "Questions can reinforce memory and reveal gaps.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaSessionTakeaway2": "Learning matters more than scoring.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaSessionTakeaway3": "A short session can still teach deeply when used well.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaSessionReflection": "Do you usually rush to answer, or do you slow down enough to learn from the question?",
  "learningJourneyTriviaReviewLessonIntro": "Review is where trivia becomes reinforcement. It helps weak questions turn into clearer understanding.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaReviewSection1Title": "What review shows you",
  "learningJourneyTriviaReviewSection1Body": "Review reveals patterns in what you forget. That makes it easier to decide whether you need more repetition or a deeper lesson.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaReviewSection2Title": "Where to go next",
  "learningJourneyTriviaReviewSection2Body": "After review, choose one related journey or tool so the quiz points back into meaningful study instead of becoming isolated.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaReviewBullet1": "Use review to spot patterns, not only isolated misses.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaReviewBullet2": "Choose one topic to revisit after the quiz.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaReviewBullet3": "Let review lead you back into the journeys.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaReviewTakeaway1": "Review turns quizzes into guidance.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaReviewTakeaway2": "Weak answers can point to your next best lesson.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaReviewTakeaway3": "Reinforcement works best when it reconnects to deeper content.",
  "learningJourneyTriviaReviewReflection": "Which wrong answer category keeps showing you the same gap in knowledge?",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhatIsLessonIntro": "Ramadan is the month in which the Qur’an was revealed and the month in which fasting was made obligatory for believers.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhatIsSection1Title": "What makes Ramadan special",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhatIsSection1Body": "Ramadan is a month of fasting, Qur’an, dua, charity, patience, and mercy. It is not only about hunger. It is a season of worship and return.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhatIsSection2Title": "How to enter the month",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhatIsSection2Body": "Begin Ramadan with reverence and hope. Let the month feel different because your intention, schedule, and attention become more worship-centered.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhatIsBullet1": "Ramadan is a month of mercy and discipline.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhatIsBullet2": "It is linked deeply to the Qur’an.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhatIsBullet3": "You enter it best with a sincere niyyah and humility.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhatIsTakeaway1": "Ramadan is a worship month before it is a food schedule.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhatIsTakeaway2": "The month is honored because Allah honored it.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhatIsTakeaway3": "Intention changes how you live the month.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhatIsReflection": "What do you most want Ramadan to change in you this year?",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhyFastLessonIntro": "Fasting trains taqwa by teaching the believer to leave what is normally permitted for the sake of Allah.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhyFastSection1Title": "The purpose of fasting",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhyFastSection1Body": "Fasting teaches restraint, gratitude, dependence on Allah, and awareness that worship is not only visible action but also hidden discipline.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhyFastSection2Title": "How purpose changes the day",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhyFastSection2Body": "When you remember why you are fasting, hunger and tiredness feel connected to worship rather than only discomfort.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhyFastBullet1": "Fasting trains self-restraint.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhyFastBullet2": "It grows gratitude for ordinary blessings.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhyFastBullet3": "It teaches worship in private and public.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhyFastTakeaway1": "Fasting is a path to taqwa.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhyFastTakeaway2": "Its purpose is spiritual, not only physical.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhyFastTakeaway3": "Remembered purpose makes hardship lighter.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanWhyFastReflection": "When fasting feels difficult, which purpose of fasting most helps you remain sincere?",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSuhoorIftarLessonIntro": "A healthy Ramadan rhythm begins before dawn and ends after sunset, but the whole day is shaped by what happens between those points.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSuhoorIftarSection1Title": "Suhoor and beginning the day",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSuhoorIftarSection1Body": "Suhoor gives strength and barakah. Beginning the day with the niyyah to fast, prayer, and remembrance helps the fast start with steadiness.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSuhoorIftarSection2Title": "Iftar and ending the day",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSuhoorIftarSection2Body": "Iftar is a moment of gratitude, dua, and relief. Keep it balanced enough that the evening still has room for prayer, Qur’an, and rest.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSuhoorIftarBullet1": "Treat suhoor as preparation, not only fuel.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSuhoorIftarBullet2": "Break the fast with gratitude and dua.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSuhoorIftarBullet3": "Keep the evening balanced enough for worship.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSuhoorIftarTakeaway1": "The daily rhythm shapes the whole Ramadan experience.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSuhoorIftarTakeaway2": "Suhoor and iftar are spiritual moments, not only meals.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSuhoorIftarTakeaway3": "A balanced evening protects worship energy.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSuhoorIftarReflection": "Which part of your Ramadan day most needs a calmer structure?",
  "learningJourneyRamadanBreaksFastLessonIntro": "Knowing what breaks the fast gives confidence and keeps worship away from both negligence and needless panic.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanBreaksFastSection1Title": "Learn the clear cases first",
  "learningJourneyRamadanBreaksFastSection1Body": "Begin with the common matters that clearly invalidate the fast. A beginner foundation does not need every detailed edge case on day one.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanBreaksFastSection2Title": "Guard the heart from anxious uncertainty",
  "learningJourneyRamadanBreaksFastSection2Body": "Do not let fasting turn into constant worry. Learn the clear rules, ask when you need help, and avoid feeding every passing doubt.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanBreaksFastBullet1": "Focus on the clear common invalidators first.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanBreaksFastBullet2": "Ask for clarity when a real confusion remains.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanBreaksFastBullet3": "Do not let doubt consume the month.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanBreaksFastTakeaway1": "Clarity protects the fast.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanBreaksFastTakeaway2": "Beginners do not need every rare scenario at once.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanBreaksFastTakeaway3": "Islam does not want worship built on constant panic.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanBreaksFastReflection": "Do you struggle more with not knowing the rules or with overthinking them?",
  "learningJourneyRamadanLaylatLessonIntro": "Laylat al-Qadr is better than a thousand months. The believer seeks it in the last nights with worship, dua, and sincerity.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanLaylatSection1Title": "Why the last nights matter",
  "learningJourneyRamadanLaylatSection1Body": "The last ten nights carry special weight because Laylat al-Qadr is hidden within them. That hiddenness encourages steady effort rather than one-night intensity.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanLaylatSection2Title": "How to seek it",
  "learningJourneyRamadanLaylatSection2Body": "Seek the night through prayer, Qur’an, dua, repentance, and quiet sincerity. Keep the focus on Allah more than on chasing signs.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanLaylatBullet1": "Increase worship across the last nights.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanLaylatBullet2": "Use dua and repentance often.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanLaylatBullet3": "Seek sincerity more than spectacle.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanLaylatTakeaway1": "Laylat al-Qadr invites sustained effort.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanLaylatTakeaway2": "The hidden night encourages sincerity and consistency.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanLaylatTakeaway3": "Simple worship done sincerely can carry immense weight.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanLaylatReflection": "What kind of worship helps your heart feel closest to Allah in the quiet hours?",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSpiritualGoalsLessonIntro": "Ramadan changes people most when they enter it with a few clear spiritual goals instead of a vague wish to do better.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSpiritualGoalsSection1Title": "Choose a few goals only",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSpiritualGoalsSection1Body": "Good goals are small enough to repeat: more Qur’an, more dhikr, more guarded speech, more dua, or stronger salah.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSpiritualGoalsSection2Title": "Keep goals linked to worship",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSpiritualGoalsSection2Body": "A goal should help you turn to Allah more steadily. If it only increases stress or comparison, make it smaller and clearer.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSpiritualGoalsBullet1": "Choose a few goals, not too many.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSpiritualGoalsBullet2": "Tie goals to real daily moments.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSpiritualGoalsBullet3": "Review them gently through the month.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSpiritualGoalsTakeaway1": "Clarity helps Ramadan feel purposeful.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSpiritualGoalsTakeaway2": "Small repeated goals are stronger than grand vague plans.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSpiritualGoalsTakeaway3": "Good goals move the heart back to Allah.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanSpiritualGoalsReflection": "Which one spiritual habit would most change your Ramadan if you protected it daily?",
  "learningJourneyRamadanMistakesLessonIntro": "Some Ramadan mistakes do not come from bad intention. They come from hurry, excess, burnout, or losing sight of the month’s purpose.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanMistakesSection1Title": "Common traps",
  "learningJourneyRamadanMistakesSection1Body": "A person may focus on food more than worship, stay up in ways that damage prayer, waste time heavily, or become harsh and impatient while fasting.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanMistakesSection2Title": "How to protect the month",
  "learningJourneyRamadanMistakesSection2Body": "Keep the month simple enough that worship remains central. Reduce one distraction, one excess habit, and one pattern of heedlessness.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanMistakesBullet1": "Do not let food planning consume the month.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanMistakesBullet2": "Protect prayer and sleep enough to keep worship steady.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanMistakesBullet3": "Treat manners and speech as part of fasting.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanMistakesTakeaway1": "Ramadan is weakened by distraction and excess.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanMistakesTakeaway2": "Good fasting includes guarding speech and conduct.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanMistakesTakeaway3": "Simplicity often protects the month better than busyness.",
  "learningJourneyRamadanMistakesReflection": "Which one Ramadan habit tends to pull you away from the real purpose of the month?",
  "learningJourneyRamadanMistakesActionStep": "Choose one distraction to reduce this Ramadan so worship has more room to breathe.",
  "learningJourneyQuranJourneyTitle": "Journey of the Qur’an",
  "learningJourneyQuranJourneySubtitle": "Open the Qur’an and begin to know it.",
  "learningJourneyQuranJourneyDescription": "Start with the Qur’an as a living source of guidance through reading, structure, themes, and practical next steps.",
  "learningJourneyQuranJourneyOutcome1": "Understand how to approach the Qur’an as guidance",
  "learningJourneyQuranJourneyOutcome2": "Build a first reading rhythm from a clear starting point",
  "learningJourneyQuranJourneyOutcome3": "Use themes, notes, and tools as support rather than distraction",
  "learningJourneyQuranJourneyWhyThisMatters": "A stable relationship with the Qur’an gives the rest of the learning journey its center.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahTitle": "Understanding Al-Fatihah",
  "learningJourneyFatihahSubtitle": "Begin with the surah you recite every day.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahDescription": "Study Al-Fatihah verse by verse as the opening of the Qur’an and the heart of daily salah.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahOutcome1": "Follow Al-Fatihah verse by verse",
  "learningJourneyFatihahOutcome2": "Connect its words to daily salah",
  "learningJourneyFatihahOutcome3": "Leave with a reflective understanding of its central themes",
  "learningJourneyFatihahWhyThisMatters": "Al-Fatihah is recited every day, so understanding it raises the meaning of salah immediately.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahsTitle": "Short Surahs Journey",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahsSubtitle": "Build familiarity with the short surahs used often in prayer.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahsDescription": "Use short surahs as an early bridge between recitation, prayer, context, and practical meaning.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahsOutcome1": "Learn the short surahs used often in prayer with context",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahsOutcome2": "Notice key themes and simple takeaways from each surah",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahsOutcome3": "Connect memorized recitation to practical reflection",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahsWhyThisMatters": "Short surahs are the easiest place to connect memorization, recitation, and meaning.",
  "learningJourneyStageQuranOpenTitle": "How to approach the Qur’an",
  "learningJourneyStageQuranOpenSummary": "Begin with a simple frame for reading the Qur’an as guidance, worship, and daily return.",
  "learningJourneyStageQuranReadTitle": "Begin reading",
  "learningJourneyStageQuranReadSummary": "Start from Al-Fatihah and learn how to make a first reading rhythm feel realistic.",
  "learningJourneyStageQuranThemesTitle": "Themes and reflection",
  "learningJourneyStageQuranThemesSummary": "Use themes and simple note-taking to notice recurring guidance without losing the main path.",
  "learningJourneyStageQuranNextStepsTitle": "Carry the Qur’an forward",
  "learningJourneyStageQuranNextStepsSummary": "Finish by choosing your next Qur’an path and a simple way to keep the relationship alive.",
  "learningJourneyStageFatihahReadTitle": "Verses 1-2: Praise and Lordship",
  "learningJourneyStageFatihahReadSummary": "Begin with the opening praise of Allah and what it means to call Him the Lord of all worlds.",
  "learningJourneyStageFatihahRecitationTitle": "Verses 3–5: mercy, judgment and worship",
  "learningJourneyStageFatihahRecitationSummary": "See how mercy, accountability, and exclusive worship sit at the center of Al-Fatihah.",
  "learningJourneyStageFatihahReflectionTitle": "Verses 6-7: Guidance and the straight path",
  "learningJourneyStageFatihahReflectionSummary": "Reflect on what it means to ask Allah for guidance every day inside salah.",
  "learningJourneyStageFatihahCompletionTitle": "Carry Al-Fatihah into salah",
  "learningJourneyStageFatihahCompletionSummary": "Gather the themes of Al-Fatihah and choose how to remember them when you stand in prayer.",
  "learningJourneyStageShortSurahIkhlasTitle": "Surah Al-Ikhlas",
  "learningJourneyStageShortSurahIkhlasSummary": "Learn the short surah of pure tawheed and why it is so central in meaning.",
  "learningJourneyStageShortSurahFalaqTitle": "Surah Al-Falaq",
  "learningJourneyStageShortSurahFalaqSummary": "Study this surah of seeking refuge and notice how it teaches protection through Allah.",
  "learningJourneyStageShortSurahNasTitle": "Surah An-Nas",
  "learningJourneyStageShortSurahNasSummary": "Learn how this short surah teaches refuge, dependence, and protection of the heart.",
  "learningJourneyStageShortSurahKafirunTitle": "Surah Al-Kafirun",
  "learningJourneyStageShortSurahKafirunSummary": "See how this short surah teaches clarity, loyalty to worship, and respectful firmness.",
  "learningJourneyStageShortSurahKawtharTitle": "Surah Al-Kawthar",
  "learningJourneyStageShortSurahKawtharSummary": "Study this short surah of abundance, gratitude, and worship through sacrifice.",
  "learningJourneyStageShortSurahCompletionTitle": "Carry short surahs into prayer",
  "learningJourneyStageShortSurahCompletionSummary": "Finish by choosing how these short surahs can deepen recitation, memory, and reflection in salah.",
  "learningJourneyStageAlphabetCompletionTitle": "Ready for reading basics",
  "learningJourneyStageAlphabetCompletionSummary": "Finish the alphabet journey by reviewing what is stable and moving into reading marks with confidence.",
  "learningJourneyStageReadingCompletionTitle": "Move into recitation understanding",
  "learningJourneyStageReadingCompletionSummary": "Finish by linking your new reading confidence to Qur’an meaning and familiar recitation.",
  "learningJourneyStageReciteCompletionTitle": "Carry meaning into worship",
  "learningJourneyStageReciteCompletionSummary": "Finish by connecting familiar phrases to prayer, dhikr, and your next Arabic or Qur’an step.",
  "learningJourneyQuranToolSearchSubtitle": "Find a passage or theme.",
  "learningJourneyQuranBookmarksSupportSubtitle": "Return to places you want to revisit after reading.",
  "learningJourneyQuranNotesSupportSubtitle": "Keep brief reflections tied to verses and passages.",
  "learningJourneyQuranOpenIntro": "The Qur’an is not only a text to browse. It is guidance, recitation, remembrance, and a daily return to Allah.",
  "learningJourneyQuranOpenSection1Title": "A simple frame",
  "learningJourneyQuranOpenSection1Body": "Begin by seeing the Qur’an as the center of guidance. You do not need to master structure on day one. You need a calm entry and a sincere relationship.",
  "learningJourneyQuranOpenSection2Title": "How to begin well",
  "learningJourneyQuranOpenSection2Body": "Start in one clear place, keep the reading gentle, and let curiosity grow after the relationship begins.",
  "learningJourneyQuranOpenBullet1": "Start with consistency, not volume.",
  "learningJourneyQuranOpenBullet2": "Use the reader and search as support, not the main path.",
  "learningJourneyQuranOpenBullet3": "Return with reverence, even if the session is short.",
  "learningJourneyQuranOpenTakeaway1": "The Qur’an should feel like a return, not a burden.",
  "learningJourneyQuranOpenTakeaway2": "A simple starting point is enough.",
  "learningJourneyQuranOpenTakeaway3": "Tools should support the relationship, not replace it.",
  "learningJourneyQuranOpenReflection": "What kind of Qur’an relationship are you trying to build: occasional browsing or steady return?",
  "learningJourneyQuranReadIntro": "A first reading rhythm should feel realistic enough to survive normal life. Slow, steady return is better than intense starts that disappear.",
  "learningJourneyQuranReadSection1Title": "Choose a clear beginning",
  "learningJourneyQuranReadSection1Body": "Al-Fatihah is an ideal starting point because it is short, central to prayer, and rich in meaning. It gives both structure and immediate relevance.",
  "learningJourneyQuranReadSection2Title": "Build a rhythm",
  "learningJourneyQuranReadSection2Body": "Tie reading to one repeatable moment. Let the habit be small enough that it survives travel, stress, and ordinary tiredness.",
  "learningJourneyQuranReadBullet1": "Keep the first reading sessions short.",
  "learningJourneyQuranReadBullet2": "Return to the same place if needed.",
  "learningJourneyQuranReadBullet3": "Use bookmarks to protect continuity.",
  "learningJourneyQuranReadTakeaway1": "Small steady reading is real progress.",
  "learningJourneyQuranReadTakeaway2": "Al-Fatihah is a strong first doorway.",
  "learningJourneyQuranReadTakeaway3": "Continuity matters more than intensity.",
  "learningJourneyQuranReadReflection": "Which moment of your day could realistically become your Qur’an anchor?",
  "learningJourneyQuranThemesIntro": "Themes help you notice that the Qur’an returns again and again to guidance, mercy, accountability, worship, patience, and hope.",
  "learningJourneyQuranThemesSection1Title": "Why themes matter",
  "learningJourneyQuranThemesSection1Body": "Themes help beginners connect verses without feeling lost. They show that the Qur’an is a coherent source of guidance, not a pile of unrelated passages.",
  "learningJourneyQuranThemesSection2Title": "Use themes without losing the path",
  "learningJourneyQuranThemesSection2Body": "Themed exploration should deepen your reading, not replace it. Use themes to notice patterns, then return to steady reading and reflection.",
  "learningJourneyQuranThemesBullet1": "Use themes to connect recurring ideas.",
  "learningJourneyQuranThemesBullet2": "Keep notes brief and meaningful.",
  "learningJourneyQuranThemesBullet3": "Return to reading after thematic exploration.",
  "learningJourneyQuranThemesTakeaway1": "Themes show the coherence of the Qur’an.",
  "learningJourneyQuranThemesTakeaway2": "Notes help retention when kept simple.",
  "learningJourneyQuranThemesTakeaway3": "Theme study should support, not fragment, the journey.",
  "learningJourneyQuranThemesReflection": "Which recurring theme do you most need from the Qur’an right now: mercy, guidance, patience, or accountability?",
  "learningJourneyQuranNextStepsIntro": "The best end to a Qur’an introduction is a practical next step. Choose one path that keeps the relationship alive after the first lessons.",
  "learningJourneyQuranNextStepsSection1Title": "What you have built",
  "learningJourneyQuranNextStepsSection1Body": "You now have a calmer frame for reading, structure, and themes. The next step is choosing how to deepen that relationship without clutter.",
  "learningJourneyQuranNextStepsSection2Title": "Choose one next direction",
  "learningJourneyQuranNextStepsSection2Body": "You might go deeper into Al-Fatihah, short surahs, or familiar recitation meaning. The key is to keep one clear path instead of opening everything at once.",
  "learningJourneyQuranNextStepsBullet1": "Choose one next Qur’an journey.",
  "learningJourneyQuranNextStepsBullet2": "Keep one reading anchor in your week.",
  "learningJourneyQuranNextStepsBullet3": "Use notes or bookmarks only where they help continuity.",
  "learningJourneyQuranNextStepsTakeaway1": "Clarity protects the relationship from clutter.",
  "learningJourneyQuranNextStepsTakeaway2": "The next step should deepen the same relationship, not replace it.",
  "learningJourneyQuranNextStepsTakeaway3": "Simple ongoing return is the real goal.",
  "learningJourneyQuranNextStepsReflection": "Which next Qur’an path feels most alive for you now: Al-Fatihah, short surahs, or familiar recitation meanings?",
  "learningJourneyQuranNextStepsActionStep": "Choose one Qur’an journey to continue this week and one day you will return to the reader again.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReadIntro": "Al-Fatihah opens with praise, gratitude, and recognition of Allah as Lord over every world and every creature.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReadSection1Title": "Verse-by-verse focus",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReadSection1Body": "“In the name of Allah” begins with dependence. “All praise is for Allah” teaches gratitude. “Lord of the worlds” reminds you that Allah cares for all creation and governs it fully.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReadSection2Title": "How it enters salah",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReadSection2Body": "These opening verses teach that prayer begins with praise before asking. They re-center the heart before the rest of the surah unfolds.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReadBullet1": "Praise comes before requests.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReadBullet2": "Lordship means care, authority, and nurture.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReadBullet3": "Opening with Allah changes the tone of prayer.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReadTakeaway1": "Al-Fatihah begins with gratitude and praise.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReadTakeaway2": "Allah’s Lordship gives the surah its foundation.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReadTakeaway3": "The opening verses prepare the heart to ask.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReadReflection": "When you begin prayer, do you feel the praise in these verses or mostly move past them quickly?",
  "learningJourneyFatihahRecitationIntro": "The middle of Al-Fatihah joins Allah’s mercy, the reality of judgment, and the believer’s promise to worship and seek help only from Him.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahRecitationSection1Title": "Verse-by-verse focus",
  "learningJourneyFatihahRecitationSection1Body": "Allah is the Most Merciful and the One who owns the Day of Judgment. Then the servant responds: You alone we worship, and You alone we ask for help.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahRecitationSection2Title": "How it enters salah",
  "learningJourneyFatihahRecitationSection2Body": "Every rak‘ah renews this promise. Salah is not only recitation. It is a repeated declaration of worship, dependence, and accountability.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahRecitationBullet1": "Mercy and judgment appear together.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahRecitationBullet2": "Ibadah and dependence belong to Allah alone.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahRecitationBullet3": "These verses are central to the meaning of prayer.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahRecitationTakeaway1": "The middle of Al-Fatihah teaches exclusive worship.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahRecitationTakeaway2": "Mercy and accountability shape the believer together.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahRecitationTakeaway3": "Salah repeats this covenant every day.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahRecitationReflection": "Which phrase feels strongest to you in prayer right now: mercy, judgment, worship, or seeking help?",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReflectionIntro": "The end of Al-Fatihah turns directly into dua: guide us to the straight path and keep us away from misguidance.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReflectionSection1Title": "Verse-by-verse focus",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReflectionSection1Body": "Guidance is not asked for once. It is asked for repeatedly because the heart always needs help remaining straight, sincere, and steady.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReflectionSection2Title": "How it enters salah",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReflectionSection2Body": "Every time you recite these verses in salah, you are making a direct request to Allah for direction, clarity, and protection.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReflectionBullet1": "Guidance is a daily need.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReflectionBullet2": "The straight path requires help from Allah.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReflectionBullet3": "Salah ends the surah with active need, not self-sufficiency.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReflectionTakeaway1": "Al-Fatihah ends as a living dua.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReflectionTakeaway2": "Repeated guidance-seeking is part of a healthy heart.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReflectionTakeaway3": "The straight path is walked with divine help.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahReflectionReflection": "When you ask for guidance in Al-Fatihah, what area of life most needs it right now?",
  "learningJourneyFatihahCompletionIntro": "You have moved through Al-Fatihah as praise, worship, and dua. Now the task is to carry those meanings into daily salah.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahCompletionSection1Title": "What you have learned",
  "learningJourneyFatihahCompletionSection1Body": "Al-Fatihah begins with praise, centers worship and dependence, and ends with guidance-seeking. It teaches a full relationship between the servant and Allah.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahCompletionSection2Title": "What to do next",
  "learningJourneyFatihahCompletionSection2Body": "Keep one meaning alive each day in prayer. Let Al-Fatihah become something you understand and feel, not only something you repeat.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahCompletionBullet1": "Choose one verse theme to remember in salah.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahCompletionBullet2": "Return to the reader when needed.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahCompletionBullet3": "Use this journey as a base for short surahs and prayer meaning.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahCompletionTakeaway1": "Al-Fatihah contains praise, worship, and dua together.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahCompletionTakeaway2": "Understanding it deepens every rak‘ah.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahCompletionTakeaway3": "The next step is lived remembrance in prayer.",
  "learningJourneyFatihahCompletionReflection": "Which theme from Al-Fatihah do you most want to carry consciously into salah this week?",
  "learningJourneyFatihahCompletionActionStep": "Before one prayer today, choose one verse from Al-Fatihah and remember its meaning before you begin.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahContextTitle": "Simple context",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahThemesTitle": "Key themes and takeaway",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahIkhlasIntro": "Surah Al-Ikhlas is short in length but immense in meaning because it teaches pure tawheed and Allah’s absolute uniqueness.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahIkhlasContext": "This surah was revealed as a direct clarification of who Allah is: One, absolutely needed by all, and unlike creation.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahIkhlasThemes": "Its key theme is pure monotheism. It teaches that Allah is unique, self-sufficient, and beyond human comparison, lineage, or dependence.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahIkhlasTakeaway1": "This surah centers pure belief in Allah’s oneness.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahIkhlasTakeaway2": "It clears away wrong ideas about Allah.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahIkhlasTakeaway3": "Its short length hides very deep meaning.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahIkhlasReflection": "How would your worship change if Allah’s uniqueness felt more present in your heart?",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahFalaqIntro": "Surah Al-Falaq teaches the believer to seek refuge in Allah from outer harms and unseen dangers.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahFalaqContext": "This surah was revealed as part of the Mu‘awwidhatayn, the two surahs of seeking refuge, and is often recited for protection.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahFalaqThemes": "Its key theme is turning to Allah for protection from harm, darkness, envy, and evil that lies beyond human control.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahFalaqTakeaway1": "Protection begins with refuge in Allah.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahFalaqTakeaway2": "The surah names real harms without producing fearfulness.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahFalaqTakeaway3": "Seeking refuge is an act of trust, not weakness.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahFalaqReflection": "When you feel vulnerable, do you remember refuge in Allah as quickly as you remember other protections?",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahNasIntro": "Surah An-Nas teaches refuge in Allah from the whispers that enter the heart and try to disturb faith, peace, and clarity.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahNasContext": "Like Al-Falaq, this surah is part of the two refuge surahs and is recited regularly for protection and spiritual steadiness.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahNasThemes": "Its key theme is protection from inner whispering, hidden harm, and the subtle influences that confuse the heart.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahNasTakeaway1": "The heart needs protection as much as the body.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahNasTakeaway2": "Allah alone can protect you from hidden whispering.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahNasTakeaway3": "This surah teaches vigilance without panic.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahNasReflection": "What kind of whispering pulls your attention away from Allah most often?",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahKafirunIntro": "Surah Al-Kafirun is a short surah of clarity in worship and respectful firmness in faith.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahKafirunContext": "It was revealed in a context where compromise in worship was proposed, and the surah answered with clear loyalty to Allah alone.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahKafirunThemes": "Its key theme is clarity in worship. It teaches that worship cannot be mixed with compromise when it comes to who is truly worshipped.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahKafirunTakeaway1": "The surah teaches clarity without aggression.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahKafirunTakeaway2": "Ibadah belongs to Allah alone.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahKafirunTakeaway3": "Respectful firmness is part of faith.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahKafirunReflection": "Where do you most need clearer boundaries in worship or values?",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahKawtharIntro": "Surah Al-Kawthar is a short surah of abundance, gratitude, and worship in response to Allah’s gifts.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahKawtharContext": "It came as consolation and honor for the Prophet ﷺ, teaching that Allah’s gifts are greater than the insults of people.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahKawtharThemes": "Its key theme is abundance from Allah and the right response to that abundance: prayer, gratitude, and sacrifice.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahKawtharTakeaway1": "Allah’s gifts are greater than people’s insults.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahKawtharTakeaway2": "Gratitude should turn into worship.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahKawtharTakeaway3": "A short surah can hold deep comfort and strength.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahKawtharReflection": "How do you usually respond when Allah gives you a blessing: gratitude, distraction, or delay?",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahCompletionIntro": "These short surahs are brief enough to memorize yet deep enough to shape prayer, protection, gratitude, and belief.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahCompletionSection1Title": "What these surahs gave you",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahCompletionSection1Body": "Together they teach tawheed, refuge, gratitude, and clarity in worship. They are not only short recitations. They are living reminders.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahCompletionSection2Title": "How to carry them forward",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahCompletionSection2Body": "Use one short surah in prayer with extra attention this week. Let meaning travel with recitation instead of staying separate from it.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahCompletionBullet1": "Choose one surah to recite with more awareness.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahCompletionBullet2": "Connect its theme to your day.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahCompletionBullet3": "Use this path as a bridge into understanding what you recite.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahCompletionTakeaway1": "Short surahs are rich in practical guidance.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahCompletionTakeaway2": "Meaning deepens recitation quickly.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahCompletionTakeaway3": "Salah becomes richer when familiar surahs are understood.",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahCompletionReflection": "Which short surah do you want to carry with more awareness in prayer this week?",
  "learningJourneyShortSurahCompletionActionStep": "Pick one short surah for your next few prayers and pause briefly before reciting it to remember its main theme.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetCompletionIntro": "You now have a foundation in letter recognition and sound repetition. The next step is learning how those letters behave inside reading.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetCompletionSection1Title": "What is stable now",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetCompletionSection1Body": "You have begun to recognize letter shapes, repeat their sounds, and return to weak points with more calm than when you started.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetCompletionSection2Title": "Where to go next",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetCompletionSection2Body": "Reading basics adds the marks and sound rules that let letters become real words. That is the natural next step after alphabet familiarity.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetCompletionBullet1": "Move forward with workable confidence.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetCompletionBullet2": "Keep short review loops alive.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetCompletionBullet3": "Let reading basics build on what you now know.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetCompletionTakeaway1": "Letter familiarity is real progress.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetCompletionTakeaway2": "Review still matters after the first journey.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetCompletionTakeaway3": "The next step is learning how reading marks guide sound.",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetCompletionReflection": "Do you feel ready to add reading marks, or do you need one more week of alphabet review?",
  "learningJourneyAlphabetCompletionActionStep": "Open Reading Basics next and carry one short alphabet review session with you this week.",
  "learningJourneyReadingCompletionIntro": "You have moved from letters to marks, pauses, doubled sounds, and joined forms. Now those skills need to connect to living recitation.",
  "learningJourneyReadingCompletionSection1Title": "What this journey built",
  "learningJourneyReadingCompletionSection1Body": "Reading marks and joined letters are no longer abstract. You now have the beginning of reading confidence and know where your weak spots still are.",
  "learningJourneyReadingCompletionSection2Title": "Where to go next",
  "learningJourneyReadingCompletionSection2Body": "The natural next step is familiar recitation meaning: understanding what you recite in prayer and Qur’an through the reading confidence you have started to build.",
  "learningJourneyReadingCompletionBullet1": "Take your new reading confidence into meaning.",
  "learningJourneyReadingCompletionBullet2": "Keep reviewing the marks that still feel weak.",
  "learningJourneyReadingCompletionBullet3": "Take the Qur’an and salah journeys next.",
  "learningJourneyReadingCompletionTakeaway1": "Reading basics is a real bridge, not a side path.",
  "learningJourneyReadingCompletionTakeaway2": "Weak spots can still travel forward with review.",
  "learningJourneyReadingCompletionTakeaway3": "Meaning becomes easier when reading feels less fragile.",
  "learningJourneyReadingCompletionReflection": "Which reading skill now feels strong enough to carry into actual recitation understanding?",
  "learningJourneyReadingCompletionActionStep": "Open Understand What You Recite next and take one reading mark you want to keep watching carefully.",
  "learningJourneyReciteFatihahActionStep": "In your next prayer, pause for one second before Al-Fatihah and remember that you are beginning with praise.",
  "learningJourneyReciteShortSurahsActionStep": "Choose one short surah you recite often and connect one clear theme to it before your next salah.",
  "learningJourneyReciteMeaningActionStep": "In your next prayer or dhikr, hold one phrase in your mind and let its meaning stay present while you say it.",
  "learningJourneyReadingCheckpointActionStep": "Choose one reading mark that still feels weak and give it one more calm practice loop before moving on.",
  "learningJourneyReciteCompletionIntro": "You have connected familiar recitation to meaning. Now the task is to let that meaning travel into worship, dhikr, and your next learning step.",
  "learningJourneyReciteCompletionSection1Title": "What changed in this journey",
  "learningJourneyReciteCompletionSection1Body": "Familiar phrases no longer need to stay empty or automatic. You now have simple anchors that can bring more attention into prayer and remembrance.",
  "learningJourneyReciteCompletionSection2Title": "What to do next",
  "learningJourneyReciteCompletionSection2Body": "Use one phrase in salah with more presence, then keep building through Qur’an journeys, dhikr routines, and Arabic learning.",
  "learningJourneyReciteCompletionBullet1": "Choose one phrase to carry into worship.",
  "learningJourneyReciteCompletionBullet2": "Keep connecting Arabic to actual usage.",
  "learningJourneyReciteCompletionBullet3": "Let meaning lead you into deeper Qur’an learning.",
  "learningJourneyReciteCompletionTakeaway1": "Meaning makes repeated phrases feel alive.",
  "learningJourneyReciteCompletionTakeaway2": "Salah and dhikr become more connected when phrases are understood.",
  "learningJourneyReciteCompletionTakeaway3": "This journey is a bridge, not an endpoint.",
  "learningJourneyReciteCompletionReflection": "Which familiar phrase do you most want to keep consciously alive in worship this week?",
  "learningJourneyReciteCompletionActionStep": "Pick one phrase from prayer or dhikr and keep its meaning present the next three times you say it.",
