  "learningJourneyIslamFoundationsTitle": "What Is Islam?",
  "learningJourneyIslamFoundationsSubtitle": "A first path through belief and the pillars.",
  "learningJourneyIslamFoundationsDescription": "Start with the meaning of Islam, who Allah is, the five pillars, and the first steady steps of Muslim life.",
  "learningJourneyIslamFoundationsOutcome1": "Understand Islam as surrender, worship, and mercy.",
  "learningJourneyIslamFoundationsOutcome2": "See the five pillars as a lived structure rather than a list.",
  "learningJourneyIslamFoundationsOutcome3": "Leave with a calm first plan for daily Muslim life.",
  "learningJourneyIslamFoundationsWhyThisMatters": "Beginners need one clear first path before they are exposed to the rest of the learning library.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesTitle": "Daily Routines",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesSubtitle": "Build your day around salah.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesDescription": "Build a realistic daily Muslim routine that begins small, anchors itself to salah, and stays sustainable.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesOutcome1": "Create a simple daily worship rhythm without overwhelm.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesOutcome2": "Use salah as the anchor for Qur’an, dhikr, and duas.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesOutcome3": "Build habits through small, repeatable actions.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesWhyThisMatters": "Many users do not need more information first. They need a realistic structure they can actually live.",
  "learningJourneyStageIslamWhatIsIslamTitle": "What is Islam?",
  "learningJourneyStageIslamWhatIsIslamSummary": "Begin with the meaning of Islam as surrender to Allah, worship, and a complete way of life.",
  "learningJourneyStageIslamWhoIsAllahTitle": "Who is Allah?",
  "learningJourneyStageIslamWhoIsAllahSummary": "Learn the first clear foundations of knowing Allah as Creator, Lord, and the One worthy of worship.",
  "learningJourneyStageIslamFivePillarsTitle": "The five pillars",
  "learningJourneyStageIslamFivePillarsSummary": "See the pillars as the practical structure that shapes a Muslim life day by day.",
  "learningJourneyStageIslamFirstStepsTitle": "Your first steps",
  "learningJourneyStageIslamFirstStepsSummary": "Finish with a calm starting plan built around prayer, learning, and beautiful character.",
  "learningJourneyStageIslamCompletionTitle": "Carry Islam into daily life",
  "learningJourneyStageIslamCompletionSummary": "Review what you have learned and choose the next steady journey in worship and connection.",
  "learningJourneyStageDailyRoutinesStartDayTitle": "Start your day with a niyyah",
  "learningJourneyStageDailyRoutinesStartDaySummary": "Build a gentle opening rhythm that begins with a niyyah, remembrance, and a realistic first step.",
  "learningJourneyStageDailyRoutinesPrayerAnchorTitle": "Let salah anchor the day",
  "learningJourneyStageDailyRoutinesPrayerAnchorSummary": "Use prayer times as the stable structure that keeps the rest of your routine from drifting.",
  "learningJourneyStageDailyRoutinesQuranAnchorTitle": "Keep a small Qur’an rhythm",
  "learningJourneyStageDailyRoutinesQuranAnchorSummary": "Choose a manageable way to read, listen, or reflect on the Qur’an every day without pressure.",
  "learningJourneyStageDailyRoutinesEveningResetTitle": "End the day with a reset",
  "learningJourneyStageDailyRoutinesEveningResetSummary": "Use evening dhikr, duas, and reflection to close the day with calm rather than drift.",
  "learningJourneyStageDailyRoutinesHabitBuildingTitle": "Build habits that last",
  "learningJourneyStageDailyRoutinesHabitBuildingSummary": "Learn how to stay consistent through small actions, gentle review, and patience with yourself.",
  "learningJourneyStageDailyRoutinesCompletionTitle": "Carry your routine forward",
  "learningJourneyStageDailyRoutinesCompletionSummary": "Review your rhythm and choose the next journey that will deepen what you are already practicing.",
  "learningJourneyIslamSection1Title": "Understand the foundation",
  "learningJourneyIslamSection2Title": "Put it into life",
  "learningJourneyIslamWhatIsIslamIntro": "Islam is not only information. It is a relationship of surrender, trust, and worship directed to Allah alone.",
  "learningJourneyIslamWhatIsIslamSection1Body": "The word Islam carries the meaning of surrendering yourself to Allah in peace. A Muslim turns to Allah with belief, worship, obedience, and hope for mercy.",
  "learningJourneyIslamWhatIsIslamSection2Body": "This means Islam shapes daily life. Salah, good character, remembrance, and learning are not separate from faith. They are how faith becomes lived.",
  "learningJourneyIslamWhatIsIslamTakeaway1": "Islam begins with surrender to Allah.",
  "learningJourneyIslamWhatIsIslamTakeaway2": "Ibadah and daily life belong together.",
  "learningJourneyIslamWhatIsIslamTakeaway3": "A steady path matters more than rushing.",
  "learningJourneyIslamWhatIsIslamReflection": "What changes when you see Islam as a lived relationship with Allah rather than a list of facts?",
  "learningJourneyIslamWhoIsAllahIntro": "Knowing Allah is the center of belief. The heart becomes steady when it knows who created it and who it is returning to.",
  "learningJourneyIslamWhoIsAllahSection1Body": "Allah is the Creator, the Provider, the Lord of all worlds, and the One worthy of worship. He is not like creation, and nothing compares to Him.",
  "learningJourneyIslamWhoIsAllahSection2Body": "When you know Allah through His perfection, mercy, and lordship, worship begins to feel rooted. Salah becomes conversation, trust, and return.",
  "learningJourneyIslamWhoIsAllahTakeaway1": "Allah alone created and sustains everything.",
  "learningJourneyIslamWhoIsAllahTakeaway2": "Nothing is equal to Allah.",
  "learningJourneyIslamWhoIsAllahTakeaway3": "Knowing Allah deepens worship and trust.",
  "learningJourneyIslamWhoIsAllahReflection": "Which name or quality of Allah helps your heart feel closest to Him right now?",
  "learningJourneyIslamFivePillarsIntro": "The five pillars give structure to Muslim life. They are not random duties. They train the heart, body, time, and wealth around worship.",
  "learningJourneyIslamFivePillarsSection1Body": "The pillars are shahadah, salah, zakat, fasting Ramadan, and Hajj for those able. Together they keep belief connected to daily action, community, and obedience.",
  "learningJourneyIslamFivePillarsSection2Body": "A beginner does not need to master every detail at once. The right first move is to understand the pillars, then begin with the ones that shape daily rhythm most directly.",
  "learningJourneyIslamFivePillarsTakeaway1": "The pillars give Islam a lived structure.",
  "learningJourneyIslamFivePillarsTakeaway2": "Salah becomes the daily anchor first.",
  "learningJourneyIslamFivePillarsTakeaway3": "Learning can happen step by step.",
  "learningJourneyIslamFivePillarsReflection": "Which pillar feels most immediate in your life, and what is one calm next step you can take with it?",
  "learningJourneyIslamFirstStepsIntro": "A strong beginning is simple, repeatable, and sincere. You do not need to carry everything at once.",
  "learningJourneyIslamFirstStepsSection1Body": "Start by protecting the daily prayers as best you can, learning a small amount regularly, and keeping a few daily duas and adhkar close.",
  "learningJourneyIslamFirstStepsSection2Body": "Good company, patience with yourself, and beautiful character matter from the beginning. Growth in Islam is not only information. It is worship with steadiness.",
  "learningJourneyIslamFirstStepsTakeaway1": "Protect the basics before adding more.",
  "learningJourneyIslamFirstStepsTakeaway2": "Consistency is more important than intensity.",
  "learningJourneyIslamFirstStepsTakeaway3": "Character is part of practicing Islam.",
  "learningJourneyIslamFirstStepsReflection": "What would a calm first week of Muslim life look like for you?",
  "learningJourneyIslamCompletionIntro": "You have built a first frame for Islam, belief, and practice. The next step is to carry that frame into daily worship and connection.",
  "learningJourneyIslamCompletionSection1Title": "What you now have",
  "learningJourneyIslamCompletionSection1Body": "You now have a simple map: know Allah, understand the pillars, and build your practice through prayer, Qur’an, duas, and character.",
  "learningJourneyIslamCompletionSection2Title": "What to do next",
  "learningJourneyIslamCompletionSection2Body": "Move into salah, Al-Fatihah, and short surahs so belief becomes something you recite, live, and return to every day.",
  "learningJourneyIslamCompletionTakeaway1": "Belief and worship now have a clear shape.",
  "learningJourneyIslamCompletionTakeaway2": "Your next journey should deepen daily practice.",
  "learningJourneyIslamCompletionTakeaway3": "A calm foundation protects long-term growth.",
  "learningJourneyIslamCompletionReflection": "Which next journey will help your faith become most lived this week?",
  "learningJourneyIslamCompletionActionStep": "Choose salah or Al-Fatihah as your next steady step.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesSection1Title": "Choose the anchor",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesSection2Title": "Keep it sustainable",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesStartDayIntro": "A daily routine becomes easier when you start the day on purpose rather than reacting to whatever comes first.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesStartDaySection1Body": "Begin with one small act that reminds you why the day matters: a short dua, a moment of dhikr, or opening the Qur’an for even a few verses.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesStartDaySection2Body": "The goal is not a perfect morning routine. The goal is a repeatable opening that points your heart back to Allah and makes the next good action easier.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesStartDayTakeaway1": "Start small enough that you can repeat it.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesStartDayTakeaway2": "Intention changes the tone of the day.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesStartDayTakeaway3": "One opening act can lead to the rest.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesStartDayReflection": "What is one opening practice you could realistically repeat tomorrow morning?",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesPrayerAnchorIntro": "Salah is the strongest daily structure a Muslim has. When prayer becomes the anchor, the rest of the routine stops floating.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesPrayerAnchorSection1Body": "Instead of treating prayer as one more task, build your day around it. Let prayer times shape when you pause, reset, and return to what matters.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesPrayerAnchorSection2Body": "This also makes other habits easier. A small Qur’an reading after Fajr, dhikr after salah, or a dua before leaving home becomes attached to something already fixed.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesPrayerAnchorTakeaway1": "Salah gives the day its structure.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesPrayerAnchorTakeaway2": "Attach small habits to salah.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesPrayerAnchorTakeaway3": "Returning to prayer helps the rest stay steady.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesPrayerAnchorReflection": "Which prayer is the easiest place for you to attach one small habit right now?",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesQuranAnchorIntro": "A daily Qur’an rhythm should feel possible, not heavy. Even a small amount can keep the relationship alive.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesQuranAnchorSection1Body": "Choose a form you can keep: a few verses after Fajr, reading one page, listening during a walk, or opening a note and writing one reflection.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesQuranAnchorSection2Body": "The point is consistency with an attentive heart. A short steady relationship with the Qur’an is better than waiting for rare ideal moments.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesQuranAnchorTakeaway1": "A small Qur’an habit is still meaningful.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesQuranAnchorTakeaway2": "Use the form that fits your real day.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesQuranAnchorTakeaway3": "Presence matters more than volume.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesQuranAnchorReflection": "What Qur’an rhythm fits your current day without creating pressure?",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesEveningResetIntro": "Evening can either scatter the heart or gently gather it again. A short reset helps the day end with remembrance.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesEveningResetSection1Body": "Use evening adhkar, a bedtime dua, or one quiet moment of gratitude and istighfar to close the day on purpose rather than in exhaustion alone.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesEveningResetSection2Body": "This kind of reset is also a mercy after imperfect days. Instead of guilt taking over, remembrance helps you return and begin again tomorrow.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesEveningResetTakeaway1": "Evening remembrance closes the day with calm.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesEveningResetTakeaway2": "A reset helps after imperfect days.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesEveningResetTakeaway3": "Closing well supports starting well tomorrow.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesEveningResetReflection": "What would help your evenings feel more like a return than a drift?",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesHabitBuildingIntro": "Good routines last when they stay merciful, realistic, and tied to purpose rather than pressure.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesHabitBuildingSection1Body": "Keep habits small at first. Repeat them in the same place or after the same prayer. Review them gently instead of treating one missed day as failure.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesHabitBuildingSection2Body": "Habit building in worship is not about control. It is about building doors back to Allah that are easy to open again and again.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesHabitBuildingTakeaway1": "Small repeated acts build stronger habits.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesHabitBuildingTakeaway2": "Tie habits to existing anchors.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesHabitBuildingTakeaway3": "Missing once should not break the whole path.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesHabitBuildingReflection": "Which one habit should stay small for now so it can actually last?",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesCompletionIntro": "You now have a simple daily rhythm. The next step is to keep deepening it without adding clutter or pressure.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesCompletionSection1Title": "What you now have",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesCompletionSection1Body": "You have a practical frame for mornings, prayer anchors, Qur’an connection, evening reset, and habit-building through small repeated actions.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesCompletionSection2Title": "What to deepen next",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesCompletionSection2Body": "Choose the next journey that strengthens what you are already doing, such as dhikr, Ramadan preparation, or beautiful character.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesCompletionTakeaway1": "A calm rhythm is better than an overloaded plan.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesCompletionTakeaway2": "The next journey should deepen what is already working.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesCompletionTakeaway3": "Routine becomes worship when it stays connected to Allah.",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesCompletionReflection": "Which practice from this journey feels most ready to become part of your normal day?",
  "learningJourneyDailyRoutinesCompletionActionStep": "Choose one habit to protect this week and one journey to deepen it.",
