  "gardenElementOceanMeaning": "A reminder that what you are walking toward has no end: the sea would run dry before the words of your Lord were exhausted.",
  "gardenElementOliveTitle": "The Olive",
  "gardenElementOliveMeaning": "The blessed tree of the Verse of Light, neither of the east nor of the west, whose oil would almost glow though no fire touched it.",
  "gardenElementDatePalmTitle": "The Date Palm",
  "gardenElementDatePalmMeaning": "Shaken toward Maryam in her hardest hour, it let down fresh ripe dates: provision arriving at exactly the moment it was needed.",
  "gardenElementFigTitle": "The Fig",
  "gardenElementFigMeaning": "By the fig and the olive. An oath sworn over small sweet things, and over understanding that ripens slowly and quietly.",
  "gardenElementPomegranateTitle": "The Pomegranate",
  "gardenElementPomegranateMeaning": "Named among the fruits of the gardens. It keeps a hundred seeds in a single shell, the way wisdom gathers from many small gains.",
  "gardenElementGrapeVineTitle": "The Grapevine",
  "gardenElementGrapeVineMeaning": "From its fruit you take good provision. This is the harvest of a habit tended patiently, season after season.",
  "gardenElementGourdTitle": "The Gourd",
  "gardenElementGourdMeaning": "Grown over Yunus as he lay weakened on the open shore: shade that arrives as pure mercy, before anyone thinks to ask for it.",
  "gardenElementLoteTreeTitle": "The Lote Tree",
  "gardenElementLoteTreeMeaning": "Sidrat al-Muntaha, the lote tree of the utmost boundary, standing at the edge of what can be reached. It appears only near the summit.",
  "gardenElementRayhanTitle": "Fragrant Rayhan",
  "gardenElementRayhanMeaning": "Sweet-scented herbs named beside the grain and the husk. Remembrance is the scent a garden carries before it comes into view.",
  "gardenElementBeeTitle": "The Bee",
  "gardenElementBeeMeaning": "Inspired to travel its paths in humility, it brings out a drink of varied colours in which there is healing. Small work, done daily.",
  "gardenElementAntTitle": "The Ant",
  "gardenElementAntMeaning": "The ant who called her people into shelter so they would not be crushed unknowingly: care and preparation on the smallest scale.",
  "gardenElementHoopoeTitle": "The Hoopoe",
  "gardenElementHoopoeMeaning": "It came to Sulayman carrying news from a land he had never seen. Knowledge, sought out patiently and carried home.",
  "gardenElementSongbirdsTitle": "Birds in Rows",
  "gardenElementSongbirdsMeaning": "All that is in the heavens and the earth glorifies Him, and the birds with wings outspread, each one already knowing its prayer.",
  "gardenElementFishTitle": "The Fish",
  "gardenElementFishMeaning": "The fish that slipped away at the meeting of the two seas, marking the place where a long journey had truly begun.",
  "gardenElementSheetSourceLabel": "In the Qur’an",
  "gardenElementSheetGrowsWithLabel": "Grows with",
