  "learnDailyWisdomEntryMercyTitle": "Mercy begins close to you",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryMercyBody": "The Prophet ﷺ showed that mercy is strongest when it appears in ordinary dealings, not only big moments.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryMercyStep": "Choose one person today who most needs gentle speech from you.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryGratitudeTitle": "Gratitude steadies the heart",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryGratitudeBody": "Shukr grows when you notice Allah’s gifts in what already surrounds you, not only in what you are still seeking.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryGratitudeStep": "At one transition today, name a blessing you usually pass over and thank Allah for it before asking for anything else.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryPatienceTitle": "Patience shapes response",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryPatienceBody": "Sabr is not passive delay. It is choosing what is pleasing to Allah when your first reaction wants something else.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryPatienceStep": "Pause once today before replying when you feel rushed or frustrated.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryMercyRestraintTitle": "Mercy can look like restraint",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryMercyRestraintBody": "Not every strong response is needed. Sometimes mercy appears when you hold back a sharp word, ease a demand, or leave space for someone else’s weakness.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryMercyRestraintStep": "In one tense moment today, lower the pressure instead of proving that you are right.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryTrustTitle": "Trust grows with action",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryTrustBody": "Tawakkul is strongest when planning and reliance on Allah move together instead of pulling apart.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryTrustStep": "Write down the next honest step in one worry, take it calmly, then leave the outcome with Allah.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionMakkahDescription": "Begin with the years when tawhid, early believers, and steady da’wah were formed under social pressure, isolation, and patient endurance.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionHijrahDescription": "Use Hijrah as the clearest example of planning carefully while relying completely on Allah.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionMadinahDescription": "See how the Prophet ﷺ shaped a society where worship, leadership, brotherhood, and justice met together.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionTurningPointsTitle": "Major turning points",
  "learnSeerahCompanionTurningPointsSubtitle": "The moments that changed the course of the Seerah.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionTurningPointsDescription": "Connect Hudaybiyyah, the Conquest of Makkah, and the Farewell Hajj to the wider arc of patience, opening, and completion in the Seerah.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionFinalSermonDescription": "Return to the final public counsel that gathered worship, dignity, and responsibility into one closing message.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionWhyItMattersTitle": "Why it matters",
  "learnSeerahCompanionNextExploreTitle": "Suggested next exploration",
  "learnSeerahCompanionMakkahWhyItMatters": "Early Makkah shows that the prophetic mission began by forming belief, early loyalty, and resilient worship before visible strength or public stability arrived.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionMakkahNextExplore": "Continue with the Makkah stage, then the ayahs revealed in Makkah.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionHijrahWhyItMatters": "Hijrah is one of the clearest Seerah examples of courage, planning, sacrifice, and tawakkul working together instead of competing.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionHijrahNextExplore": "Open the Hijrah stage, then place it in the history timeline.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionMadinahWhyItMatters": "Madinah shows Islam lived as worship, brotherhood, justice, consultation, and public responsibility rather than private belief alone.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionMadinahNextExplore": "Open the Madinah Society stage, then the hadith and ayahs on life in the community.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionTurningPointsWhyItMatters": "The turning points of the Seerah help you see that treaties, openings, and closing public moments were not isolated events, but stages in how Allah opened the mission outward.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionTurningPointsNextExplore": "Use the Historical Calendar timeline first, then move through Hudaybiyyah, the Conquest of Makkah, and the Farewell Hajj to keep those moments connected to the Prophetic path itself.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionFinalSermonWhyItMatters": "The Final Sermon and Farewell Hajj gather worship, dignity, justice, covenant, and trust into one closing Seerah frame that still speaks directly to public Muslim life today.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionFinalSermonNextExplore": "Reopen the Final Sermon stage, then read the hadith and ayahs behind its principles.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionProphetsSourceSubtitle": "The Seerah beside the stories of the other prophets.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionHadithSourceSubtitle": "Hadith that bring the Seerah’s lessons into practice.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionHistorySourceSubtitle": "The history timeline around the Seerah.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionQuranSourceSubtitle": "The ayahs behind the Seerah.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionExploreJourneyDescription": "Reopen the full guided Seerah path for the whole story in order.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionExploreTimelineDescription": "Move outward into the wider history timeline to see how Hudaybiyyah, the Conquest of Makkah, and the Farewell Hajj connect to the broader Muslim story.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionHudaybiyyahTitle": "Hudaybiyyah",
  "learnSeerahCompanionHudaybiyyahSubtitle": "The treaty that looked like a loss, and opened the way.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionHudaybiyyahDescription": "Use Hudaybiyyah to see how restraint, covenant, and long vision can become victory before visible conquest appears.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionHudaybiyyahWhyItMatters": "Hudaybiyyah teaches that not every apparent setback is loss. Some openings arrive through patience, disciplined agreement, and trust that Allah is shaping a larger outcome.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionHudaybiyyahNextExplore": "Open the history timeline, then the hadith on patience and keeping covenants.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionConquestTitle": "Conquest of Makkah",
  "learnSeerahCompanionConquestSubtitle": "The opening of Makkah, when strength came with mercy.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionConquestDescription": "Use this moment to see how the Prophet ﷺ entered Makkah with humility and restraint when outward victory finally arrived.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionConquestWhyItMatters": "The Conquest of Makkah shows that prophetic victory is not driven by revenge. It is marked by tawhid, mercy, and the disciplined use of power.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionConquestNextExplore": "Open the history timeline, then the Prophets and hadith.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionFarewellHajjTitle": "Farewell Hajj",
  "learnSeerahCompanionFarewellHajjSubtitle": "The last pilgrimage, and the completion of the mission.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionFarewellHajjDescription": "Use Farewell Hajj as the closing movement of the Seerah before the Final Sermon, when the Prophet ﷺ gathered the community in worship and final counsel.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionFarewellHajjWhyItMatters": "Farewell Hajj matters because it joins worship, unity, accountability, and final prophetic instruction in one public moment near the completion of the mission.",
  "learnSeerahCompanionFarewellHajjNextExplore": "Reopen the Final Sermon stage, then follow hadith and Qur’an-linked study so the closing pilgrimage stays connected to its lasting guidance.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionHeroNote": "Beautiful character grows through repeated choices in family, speech, intention, anger, mercy, and consistency.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionIkhlasDescription": "Keep intentions clean by seeking Allah’s pleasure before recognition, praise, or quick results.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionIkhlasPracticalExpression": "Pause before a good deed, service, or study effort and ask whether your heart is still facing Allah more than image, praise, or momentum.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionIkhlasNextStep": "Open the intentions scenario, then revisit the ikhlas journey stage when your worship or service starts to feel performative.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionSabrDescription": "Practice patience by staying steady in hardship, worship, and dealing with people.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionSabrPracticalExpression": "Hold your response a little longer than your emotion wants, especially when hardship, delay, or irritation makes quick reaction feel easier.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionSabrNextStep": "Move into the consistency scenario, then return to the sabr journey stage for steadiness in worship and daily pressure.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionShukrDescription": "Let gratitude show through words, worship, and the way blessings are used.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionShukrPracticalExpression": "Turn appreciation into action by using a blessing with care, naming it to Allah, and letting it improve the way you treat people around you.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionShukrNextStep": "Start with the family scenario, then revisit the shukr journey stage when blessings begin to feel ordinary.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionHumilityDescription": "Lower the ego so truth, service, and respect can stay stronger than self-importance.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionHumilityPracticalExpression": "Make room for correction, listen without protecting your ego, and let service matter more than being noticed.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionHumilityNextStep": "Use the neighbors and community scenario, then return to the humility journey stage when status or defensiveness starts leading the moment.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionForgivenessDescription": "Hold people accountable when needed without letting resentment become your inner tone.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionForgivenessPracticalExpression": "Refuse to keep feeding an old hurt with repeated inner replay, even while you still set wise boundaries and speak truthfully.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionForgivenessNextStep": "Walk through the family scenario, then reopen the forgiveness journey stage when a wound starts shaping your tone more than mercy does.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionAngerDescription": "Respond slowly when anger rises so strength is measured by restraint rather than reaction.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionAngerPracticalExpression": "Notice the first heat in your body and slow your voice, your pace, and your words before the moment becomes heavier.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionAngerNextStep": "Open the scenario on anger, then the journey stage on restraint.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionKindnessDescription": "Make gentleness visible in tone, timing, and the way you carry people’s weaknesses.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionKindnessPracticalExpression": "Choose a softer tone, better timing, and more considerate words so truth lands without harshness or contempt.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionKindnessNextStep": "Begin with the scenario on speech, then the journey stage on kindness.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioFamilyDescription": "Bring adab into everyday tension, caregiving, and small family conversations.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioFamilyPracticalExpression": "Practice patience, soft speech, and quiet service at home before looking for character tests in bigger public moments.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioFamilyNextStep": "Open Divine Life family lessons when home responsibilities, tension, or caregiving need more practical examples.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioSpeechDescription": "Use fewer words, clearer truth, and more gentleness when speaking under pressure.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioSpeechPracticalExpression": "Lower the temperature of your speech first, then choose words that stay truthful without becoming sharp, loud, or excessive.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioSpeechNextStep": "Open Qur’an reflection on character and adab for ayah-guided restraint, timing, and mercy in speech.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioNeighborsDescription": "Treat neighbors and shared spaces as a real test of adab through reliability, quiet kindness, patient boundaries, and the way people feel around you.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioNeighborsPracticalExpression": "Notice the ordinary neighbor rights people remember most: greeting well, keeping noise and harm in check, offering small help, respecting privacy, and staying patient when irritation is minor.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioNeighborsNextStep": "Move into Divine Life community lessons when shared space, small tensions, or overlooked neighbor duties need fuller practical examples.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioConsistencyDescription": "Keep good conduct alive through small regular actions instead of waiting for ideal moods, strong energy, or a perfect spiritual moment.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioConsistencyPracticalExpression": "Choose one steady behavior you can keep on tired, rushed, or low-motivation days, because character deepens more through repeatable faithfulness than occasional intensity.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioConsistencyNextStep": "Open Qur’an guidance for daily life to find steadiness in worship, manners, and routine conduct as your energy rises and falls.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioWorkStudyTitle": "Work and study pressure",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioWorkStudySubtitle": "Carry adab, intention, and restraint into deadlines, stress, and busy seasons.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioWorkStudyDescription": "Use this scenario when workload, deadlines, or academic pressure start squeezing sincerity, patience, speech, and presence with people.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioWorkStudyPracticalExpression": "Slow the rush just enough to renew your intention, lower your tone, and protect one steady act of worship or good conduct even when the day feels compressed.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioWorkStudyNextStep": "Open Divine Life trust and effort themes when pressure, decisions, or busy seasons need more Qur’an-rooted perspective on calm excellence and reliance.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioIntentionsTitle": "Intentions",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioIntentionsSubtitle": "Begin actions by checking who they are really for.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioIntentionsDescription": "Return to sincerity whenever worship, service, or learning starts to drift toward image or habit.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioIntentionsPracticalExpression": "Name the act you are about to do, then quietly renew who it is for before habit, image, or public notice starts steering it.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioIntentionsNextStep": "Open the hadith intention theme when sincerity needs direct prophetic reminders about why actions are judged by intention.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioAngerTitle": "Anger and self-control",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioAngerSubtitle": "Slow the first reaction so strength stays tied to taqwa.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioAngerDescription": "Practice restraint before words and decisions make a hard moment heavier.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioAngerPracticalExpression": "Interrupt the first surge with silence, breath, or physical pause so your strength shows in restraint before speech becomes harm.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionScenarioAngerNextStep": "Open the hadith character and manners theme for direct prophetic guidance on restraint, gentleness, and measured strength.",
  "learnCharacterCompanionHadithSourceSubtitle": "Use hadith themes and collections when character and manners need direct prophetic guidance.",
