  "learnDailyWisdomSourceReflectionSubtitle": "Your saved reflections on the Qur’an.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryIntentionTitle": "Intention changes the weight of an action",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryIntentionBody": "A small act done for Allah can become heavier than a visible act done for the self. Sincerity protects good work from becoming self-display.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryIntentionStep": "Before one routine action today, pause and quietly renew your intention for Allah alone.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryHumilityTitle": "Humility leaves room for truth",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryHumilityBody": "A humble heart does not become smaller by accepting correction. It becomes freer from the need to protect image, status, or the last word.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryHumilityStep": "Let one person finish today without interrupting, correcting, or pulling the moment back toward yourself.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryServiceTitle": "Service often begins in small unseen ways",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryServiceBody": "Acts of service are often most sincere when they lighten someone’s burden quietly, before they become visible or praised.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryServiceStep": "Do one useful thing for someone today without announcing it or waiting to be noticed.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryRemembranceTitle": "Remembrance returns the heart to balance",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryRemembranceBody": "Dhikr does not remove every pressure at once, but it keeps the heart from being ruled by pressure alone. Remembering Allah changes the weight of a moment.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryRemembranceStep": "Pause for one short dhikr phrase before your next busy transition and let it slow your heart down.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryRemembranceSettlingTitle": "Remembrance can settle a scattered hour",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryRemembranceSettlingBody": "Some days do not need more force. They need the heart returned to Allah often enough that worry stops speaking as if it is the only thing that matters.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryRemembranceSettlingStep": "Choose one repeated pause today, such as before opening a message or starting the car, and pair it with a quiet dhikr phrase.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryHopeTitle": "Hope keeps repentance open",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryHopeBody": "A believer does not ignore mistakes, but does not close the door of mercy either. Hope keeps the heart moving back to Allah instead of sinking into despair.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryHopeStep": "Bring one mistake to Allah today with istighfar and a real intention to return better.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryHopeOpeningTitle": "Openings sometimes arrive after waiting",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryHopeOpeningBody": "The Seerah reminds us that not every delay is abandonment. Some openings come after patience, restraint, and trust have already done their quiet work.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryHopeOpeningStep": "When something feels delayed today, ask what faithful patience is still required from you before asking why the opening has not arrived yet.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryReflectionTitle": "Reflection turns reminders into guidance",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryReflectionBody": "A reminder settles more deeply when you stop with it, revisit it, and let it ask something of your heart instead of passing by quickly.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryReflectionStep": "After one prayer, return to one ayah or note and ask what it asks of your heart.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryForgivenessTitle": "Forgiveness keeps the heart light",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryForgivenessBody": "Letting go is not always denying harm. Often it is refusing to let bitterness keep shaping your inner life after the moment has passed.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryForgivenessStep": "Name one hurt you can stop rehearsing today, and replace one replay of it with a quiet dua for healing or justice.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryServicePresenceTitle": "Service begins with being present",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryServicePresenceBody": "Helping well is not always solving quickly. Sometimes service begins by noticing who is carrying strain alone and staying present before offering the next useful act.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntryServicePresenceStep": "Stay a little longer with one person who seems burdened today before deciding what help would actually ease things.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntrySteadinessTitle": "Small steadiness outlasts intensity",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntrySteadinessBody": "A calm regular act often carries further than a burst of effort that disappears quickly. What stays with Allah is what stays sincere and sustainable.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntrySteadinessStep": "Choose the smallest act you can repeat for three ordinary days, not just one inspired moment.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntrySpeechTitle": "Speech reveals what the heart is carrying",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntrySpeechBody": "Words can heal, expose ego, or deepen tension in seconds. Good speech is not only true; it is timely, measured, and merciful.",
  "learnDailyWisdomEntrySpeechStep": "Before one difficult conversation today, decide the first gentle sentence you want to begin with.",
