  "salahTrainerPrayerFajrTitle": "Fajr",
  "salahTrainerPrayerFajrDescription": "The opening prayer of the day, prayed before sunrise.",
  "salahTrainerPrayerFajrSunnahRakahs": "2 Sunnah",
  "salahTrainerPrayerFajrFardRakahs": "2 Fard",
  "salahTrainerPrayerFajrRecitationStyle": "Loud recitation in the fard prayer.",
  "salahTrainerPrayerFajrOverview": "Fajr begins the day with calmness, clarity, and dependence on Allah. The guided trainer focuses on the 2 fard rakahs while still showing the sunnah overview.",
  "salahTrainerPrayerDhuhrTitle": "Dhuhr",
  "salahTrainerPrayerDhuhrDescription": "The midday prayer offered after the sun passes its peak.",
  "salahTrainerPrayerDhuhrSunnahRakahs": "4 Sunnah before, 2 Sunnah after",
  "salahTrainerPrayerDhuhrFardRakahs": "4 Fard",
  "salahTrainerPrayerDhuhrRecitationStyle": "Silent recitation.",
  "salahTrainerPrayerDhuhrOverview": "Dhuhr centers the middle of the day. The guided trainer follows the 4 fard rakahs, with the first two including an additional surah after al-Fatihah.",
  "salahTrainerPrayerAsrTitle": "Asr",
  "salahTrainerPrayerAsrDescription": "The late afternoon prayer before sunset.",
  "salahTrainerPrayerAsrSunnahRakahs": "4 Sunnah optional before",
  "salahTrainerPrayerAsrFardRakahs": "4 Fard",
  "salahTrainerPrayerAsrRecitationStyle": "Silent recitation.",
  "salahTrainerPrayerAsrOverview": "Asr is a prayer of steadfastness. The trainer keeps the structure simple and repeatable so the user can focus on calm movement and consistency.",
  "salahTrainerPrayerMaghribTitle": "Maghrib",
  "salahTrainerPrayerMaghribDescription": "The sunset prayer offered immediately after sunset.",
  "salahTrainerPrayerMaghribSunnahRakahs": "2 Sunnah after",
  "salahTrainerPrayerMaghribFardRakahs": "3 Fard",
  "salahTrainerPrayerMaghribRecitationStyle": "Loud in the first two rakahs, quieter in the third.",
  "salahTrainerPrayerMaghribOverview": "Maghrib closes the day quickly after sunset. The first two rakahs include an added surah; the third rakah returns to al-Fatihah only before the final sitting.",
  "salahTrainerPrayerIshaTitle": "Isha",
  "salahTrainerPrayerIshaDescription": "The night prayer that closes the daily five prayers.",
  "salahTrainerPrayerIshaSunnahRakahs": "2 Sunnah after",
  "salahTrainerPrayerIshaFardRakahs": "4 Fard",
  "salahTrainerPrayerIshaRecitationStyle": "Loud in the first two rakahs, quieter in the last two.",
  "salahTrainerPrayerIshaOverview": "Isha closes the day with stillness. The trainer walks through the 4 fard rakahs and is designed to pair well with slower recitation practice at night.",
  "salahTrainerPrayerWitrTitle": "Witr",
  "salahTrainerPrayerWitrDescription": "The odd-numbered night prayer prayed after Isha before sleep or before Fajr.",
  "salahTrainerPrayerWitrSunnahRakahs": "Night prayer and Witr",
  "salahTrainerPrayerWitrFardRakahs": "Commonly 1 or 3 Witr",
  "salahTrainerPrayerWitrRecitationStyle": "Usually audible enough to hear yourself at night.",
  "salahTrainerPrayerWitrOverview": "Witr closes the night prayer with an odd number of rakahs. This trainer models a common 3-rakah flow and includes Qunut guidance in the final rakah.",
  "salahTrainerWitrGuidanceHanafi": "Hanafi guidance commonly treats Witr as 3 rakahs together, with Qunut after the surah in the third rakah before ruku.",
  "salahTrainerWitrGuidanceShafii": "Shafi’i guidance allows 1 or 3 rakahs of Witr, with Qunut commonly associated with the latter part of Ramadan in Fajr and variations in Witr practice.",
  "salahTrainerWitrGuidanceMaliki": "Maliki practice commonly emphasizes Witr as a distinct odd closing prayer, often prayed as one rakah after shaf.",
  "salahTrainerWitrGuidanceHanbali": "Hanbali guidance allows multiple valid forms of Witr, including 1, 3, 5, and more, while keeping the prayer odd-numbered.",
  "salahTrainerWitrNote1": "Valid Witr forms differ across madhhabs and established teaching traditions.",
  "salahTrainerWitrNote2": "This shows one common way to pray it, not the only valid one.",
  "salahTrainerPrayerJummahTitle": "Jumu’ah",
  "salahTrainerPrayerJummahDescription": "The Friday congregational prayer that replaces Dhuhr for those obligated to attend.",
  "salahTrainerPrayerJummahSunnahRakahs": "Sunnah before and after vary",
  "salahTrainerPrayerJummahFardRakahs": "2 Fard after khutbah",
  "salahTrainerPrayerJummahRecitationStyle": "Recited aloud in congregation.",
  "salahTrainerPrayerJummahOverview": "Jumu’ah includes the khutbah before the prayer and two rakahs prayed in congregation. This guide focuses on the two prayer rakahs and reminds you of the khutbah context.",
  "salahTrainerJummahGuidanceHanafi": "Hanafi guidance emphasizes the congregational obligation, khutbah conditions, and attending before the imam ascends the pulpit.",
  "salahTrainerJummahGuidanceShafii": "Shafi’i guidance places detailed conditions on congregation size, khutbah order, and settlement context.",
  "salahTrainerJummahGuidanceMaliki": "Maliki guidance emphasizes the imam-led khutbah, congregation, and the public nature of Jumu’ah.",
  "salahTrainerJummahGuidanceHanbali": "Hanbali guidance emphasizes congregational attendance, khutbah attentiveness, and the replacement of Dhuhr by Jumu’ah for those obligated.",
  "salahTrainerJummahNote1": "Jumu’ah includes two khutbahs before the prayer itself.",
  "salahTrainerJummahNote2": "If you miss Jumu’ah, or it isn’t obligatory for you, pray Dhuhr instead.",
