  "salahTrainerEssentialConditionsTitle": "Conditions of salah",
  "salahTrainerEssentialConditionsSummary": "Before salah begins, the foundations around it must be in place.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialConditionsBullet1": "Salah time must have entered.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialConditionsBullet2": "The body, clothing, and place of salah should be clean.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialConditionsBullet3": "Awrah should be covered appropriately.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialConditionsBullet4": "Face the qiblah as best as you can.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialConditionsBullet5": "Make the intention in the heart for the salah you are offering.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialInvalidatorsTitle": "What invalidates salah",
  "salahTrainerEssentialInvalidatorsSummary": "Some things break salah and require starting again.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialInvalidatorsBullet1": "Breaking wudu invalidates the salah.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialInvalidatorsBullet2": "Intentional speaking unrelated to salah invalidates it.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialInvalidatorsBullet3": "Large unnecessary movements break the calmness and can invalidate salah.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialInvalidatorsBullet4": "Intentionally eating or drinking invalidates salah.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialInvalidatorsBullet5": "Losing awareness of the salah entirely or deliberately turning away from the qiblah invalidates it.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialLoudSilentTitle": "Loud vs silent salahs",
  "salahTrainerEssentialLoudSilentSummary": "Some salahs are recited aloud in the fard salah and others silently.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialLoudSilentBullet1": "Fajr is recited aloud.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialLoudSilentBullet2": "Maghrib and Isha are recited aloud in the first two rakahs.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialLoudSilentBullet3": "Dhuhr and Asr are recited silently.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialLoudSilentBullet4": "A person praying alone may still follow the normal style of the salah.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialMistakesTitle": "Common beginner mistakes",
  "salahTrainerEssentialMistakesSummary": "Many mistakes come from rushing or uncertainty rather than neglect.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialMistakesBullet1": "Rushing through ruku and sujud without pausing calmly.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialMistakesBullet2": "Not standing fully after ruku before going down to sujud.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialMistakesBullet3": "Forgetting that al-Fatihah is recited in every rakah.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialMistakesBullet4": "Confusing the final sitting with the middle sitting in 3- and 4-rakah prayers.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialMistakesBullet5": "Letting worry about perfection remove the calmness of salah.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialIntentionTimingTitle": "Intention and salah timing",
  "salahTrainerEssentialIntentionTimingSummary": "Salah is strongest when offered on time and with khushu.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialIntentionTimingBullet1": "Intention is a quiet inward act, not a required spoken formula.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialIntentionTimingBullet2": "Try to pray early in the prayer window when possible.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialIntentionTimingBullet3": "Build consistency before chasing complexity.",
  "salahTrainerEssentialIntentionTimingBullet4": "If you are learning, steady accuracy matters more than speed.",
  "salahTrainerSurahAlFatihahSummary": "The opening surah recited in every rakah of salah.",
  "salahTrainerSurahAlFatihahReflection": "Al-Fatihah gathers praise, worship, dependence, and dua into one foundational surah repeated throughout the day.",
  "salahTrainerSurahAlFilSummary": "A short surah about the defeat of the army of the elephant.",
  "salahTrainerSurahAlFilReflection": "This surah strengthens trust that Allah protects His sacred signs and can overturn overwhelming power.",
  "salahTrainerSurahQurayshSummary": "A reminder to Quraysh to worship the Lord who secured and provided for them.",
  "salahTrainerSurahQurayshReflection": "This surah joins gratitude to worship. Security and provision should deepen obedience, not forgetfulness.",
  "salahTrainerSurahAlMaunSummary": "A warning against neglecting prayer and withholding small acts of care.",
  "salahTrainerSurahAlMaunReflection": "Salah without mercy and sincerity becomes hollow. This surah keeps ibadah tied to character.",
  "salahTrainerSurahAlKawtharSummary": "A short surah of abundance, salah, and sacrifice for Allah alone.",
  "salahTrainerSurahAlKawtharReflection": "This surah teaches the heart to answer blessing with salah and sincere devotion.",
  "salahTrainerSurahAlKafirunSummary": "A clear declaration of worshipping Allah alone without compromise.",
  "salahTrainerSurahAlKafirunReflection": "This surah steadies intention. Ibadah belongs to Allah alone, without negotiation or blending.",
  "salahTrainerSurahAnNasrSummary": "A surah about Allah’s help, victory, and ending success with praise and repentance.",
  "salahTrainerSurahAnNasrReflection": "Even in victory, the believer responds with tasbih, gratitude, and repentance rather than self-congratulation.",
